1
00:00:03,780 --> 00:00:06,916
[man speaks Sardaukar]

2
00:00:11,421 --> 00:00:13,689
[slow dramatic music playing]

3
00:00:42,652 --> 00:00:44,954
[rhythmic thumping music
playing]

4
00:00:55,298 --> 00:00:57,600
[girl in English]  My planet
Arrakis is so beautiful

5
00:00:57,667 --> 00:00:59,235
when the sun is low.

6
00:01:02,605 --> 00:01:05,141
Rolling over the sands...

7
00:01:05,241 --> 00:01:08,144
you can see spice in the air.

8
00:01:13,616 --> 00:01:15,418
[inhuman growl]

9
00:01:20,423 --> 00:01:24,460
At nightfall,
the spice harvesters land.

10
00:01:25,795 --> 00:01:28,097
The outsiders
race against time

11
00:01:28,164 --> 00:01:30,500
to avoid the heat of the day.

12
00:01:34,203 --> 00:01:36,339
[thumping music tempo
increasing]

13
00:01:39,375 --> 00:01:43,279
They ravage our lands
in front of our eyes.

14
00:01:43,346 --> 00:01:47,283
Their cruelty to my people
is all I've known.

15
00:01:47,350 --> 00:01:49,352
[dramatic music playing]

16
00:01:51,954 --> 00:01:54,390
These outsiders,
the Harkonnens,

17
00:01:54,490 --> 00:01:56,492
came long before I was born.

18
00:01:56,559 --> 00:01:58,494
By controlling
spice production,

19
00:01:58,561 --> 00:02:00,396
they became obscenely rich.

20
00:02:00,496 --> 00:02:03,199
Richer than
the Emperor himself.

21
00:02:04,367 --> 00:02:05,501
[exhales sharply]

22
00:02:20,650 --> 00:02:22,385
-[stabs]
-[man screaming]

23
00:02:24,353 --> 00:02:25,721
[gunshot]

24
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:32,328
[explosions]

25
00:02:36,732 --> 00:02:38,067
[screaming]

26
00:02:44,874 --> 00:02:48,377
Our warriors couldn't free
Arrakis from the Harkonnens,

27
00:02:48,444 --> 00:02:49,679
but one day,

28
00:02:49,745 --> 00:02:53,082
by Imperial decree,
they were gone.

29
00:02:59,722 --> 00:03:02,358
Why did the Emperor
choose this path?

30
00:03:03,626 --> 00:03:06,128
And who will
our next oppressors be?

31
00:03:15,638 --> 00:03:17,306
[inhales deeply]

32
00:03:26,649 --> 00:03:28,551
[breathes deeply]

33
00:03:44,066 --> 00:03:45,901
[soft music playing]

34
00:03:57,413 --> 00:03:59,148
[Lady Jessica]
It's good you're up early.

35
00:04:00,516 --> 00:04:01,851
Your father wants you
in full dress

36
00:04:01,951 --> 00:04:03,653
before the Emperor's Herald
arrives.

37
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:05,821
Full dress?

38
00:04:06,756 --> 00:04:08,424
Military?

39
00:04:08,491 --> 00:04:11,027
-Ceremonial.
-[Paul sighs]

40
00:04:11,127 --> 00:04:12,361
Why do we have to go
through all this

41
00:04:12,461 --> 00:04:13,963
when it's already
been decided?

42
00:04:15,031 --> 00:04:16,432
Ceremony.

43
00:04:17,133 --> 00:04:18,134
Mm.

44
00:04:19,001 --> 00:04:20,036
Thank you.

45
00:04:21,504 --> 00:04:23,873
If you want it,
make me give it to you.

46
00:04:25,274 --> 00:04:26,175
Use the Voice.

47
00:04:26,275 --> 00:04:28,110
Mom, I just woke up.

48
00:04:36,319 --> 00:04:38,354
Give me the water.

49
00:04:38,454 --> 00:04:40,723
The glass can't hear you.
Command me.

50
00:04:58,341 --> 00:05:00,843
[wind chimes tinkling]

51
00:05:07,917 --> 00:05:10,186
[distorted voice]
Give me the water.

52
00:05:16,692 --> 00:05:18,761
[wind chimes stops tinkling]

53
00:05:22,665 --> 00:05:23,666
Almost.

54
00:05:23,733 --> 00:05:25,101
[normal voice] Almost?

55
00:05:25,201 --> 00:05:27,603
Bene Gesserit skills
take years to learn, Paul.

56
00:05:27,703 --> 00:05:30,573
-[Paul] Mm-hmm.
-You look tired.

57
00:05:31,540 --> 00:05:32,775
More dreams?

58
00:05:38,381 --> 00:05:39,448
No.

59
00:05:42,218 --> 00:05:44,053
[narrator over speakers]
Extreme temperatures

60
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:45,788
and treacherous weather events

61
00:05:45,888 --> 00:05:49,625
make life outside the cities
of Arrakis truly hostile,

62
00:05:49,725 --> 00:05:51,594
with sandstorms
powerful enough

63
00:05:51,694 --> 00:05:53,295
to cut through metal.

64
00:05:53,396 --> 00:05:56,098
Only the native tribes
known as the Fremen

65
00:05:56,198 --> 00:05:59,769
have adapted
well enough to survive.

66
00:05:59,869 --> 00:06:04,306
Preferring to inhabit the
remotest regions of Arrakis,

67
00:06:04,407 --> 00:06:06,308
the Fremen share
the deep desert

68
00:06:06,409 --> 00:06:07,977
with the giant sandworms

69
00:06:08,077 --> 00:06:11,480
known to the Fremen
as  Shai-Hulud.

70
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:14,150
Long exposure to spice
has given the tribe

71
00:06:14,250 --> 00:06:16,919
their characteristic
blue eyes,

72
00:06:16,986 --> 00:06:18,954
the Eyes of Ibad.

73
00:06:19,054 --> 00:06:22,057
Little else is known
of the Fremen,

74
00:06:22,124 --> 00:06:26,162
except that they are
dangerous and unreliable.

75
00:06:26,262 --> 00:06:28,964
Fremen attacks
make spice harvesting

76
00:06:29,064 --> 00:06:30,933
extremely hazardous.

77
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:34,670
For the Fremen, spice
is the sacred hallucinogen

78
00:06:34,770 --> 00:06:36,105
which preserves life

79
00:06:36,172 --> 00:06:38,974
and brings
enormous health benefits.

80
00:06:39,074 --> 00:06:40,676
For the Imperium,

81
00:06:40,776 --> 00:06:42,912
spice is used
by the navigators

82
00:06:42,978 --> 00:06:44,680
of the Spacing Guild

83
00:06:44,780 --> 00:06:47,650
to find safe paths
between the stars.

84
00:06:47,750 --> 00:06:48,951
Without spice,

85
00:06:49,018 --> 00:06:52,021
interstellar travel
is impossible,

86
00:06:52,121 --> 00:06:53,589
making it by far

87
00:06:53,656 --> 00:06:56,859
the most valuable substance
in the universe.

88
00:06:56,959 --> 00:06:58,828
[slow dramatic music playing]

89
00:07:26,188 --> 00:07:27,890
[slow dramatic music
continues]

90
00:07:46,308 --> 00:07:47,343
Smile, Gurney.

91
00:07:48,477 --> 00:07:50,513
I am smiling.

92
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:53,082
How much will it cost them,

93
00:07:53,182 --> 00:07:55,684
traveling all this way
for this formality?

94
00:07:55,751 --> 00:07:57,086
Three Guild Navigators.

95
00:07:57,186 --> 00:08:00,856
A total of 1.46 million,
62 solaris, round trip.

96
00:08:16,572 --> 00:08:19,842
By the grace of
Shaddam IV of House Corrino,

97
00:08:19,909 --> 00:08:21,877
ascendant to
the Golden Lion Throne

98
00:08:21,944 --> 00:08:24,780
of Padishah Emperor
of the Known Universe,

99
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:29,118
I stand before you
as Herald of the Change.

100
00:08:29,218 --> 00:08:32,121
We are witnessed by members
of the Imperial Court,

101
00:08:32,221 --> 00:08:34,723
representatives
of the Spacing Guild

102
00:08:34,790 --> 00:08:38,093
and a sister
of the Bene Gesserit.

103
00:08:39,562 --> 00:08:41,864
The Emperor has spoken.

104
00:08:43,299 --> 00:08:46,101
"House Atreides
shall immediately

105
00:08:46,201 --> 00:08:47,937
take control of Arrakis

106
00:08:48,037 --> 00:08:51,206
and serve as its steward."

107
00:08:52,908 --> 00:08:54,810
Do you accept?

108
00:09:03,986 --> 00:09:06,889
[Leto] We are House Atreides.

109
00:09:06,956 --> 00:09:08,891
There is no call
we do not answer,

110
00:09:08,958 --> 00:09:11,293
there is no faith
that we betray.

111
00:09:11,393 --> 00:09:16,398
The Emperor asks us
to bring peace to Arrakis.

112
00:09:16,465 --> 00:09:18,901
House Atreides accepts.

113
00:09:18,968 --> 00:09:23,339
[officers chanting]
Atreides! Atreides! Atreides!

114
00:09:23,439 --> 00:09:27,910
Atreides! Atreides! Atreides!

115
00:09:34,950 --> 00:09:36,518
Your seal.

116
00:10:12,287 --> 00:10:13,555
So, it's done?

117
00:10:15,190 --> 00:10:16,659
It's done.

118
00:10:43,318 --> 00:10:44,720
[Lanville] How was it?

119
00:10:44,820 --> 00:10:46,221
[Duncan over mask]
Stabilizers are too loose.

120
00:10:46,321 --> 00:10:48,390
-We'll dial it in.
-Thank you, my friend.

121
00:10:48,490 --> 00:10:49,558
[Lanville] Got it.

122
00:10:50,225 --> 00:10:51,260
[Paul] Duncan.

123
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:52,428
[Duncan]  My boy.

124
00:10:52,528 --> 00:10:53,929
-[Duncan chuckles]
-Hey. Hey.

125
00:10:54,029 --> 00:10:55,564
[Duncan]  Paul, my boy.

126
00:10:57,266 --> 00:10:59,735
So, you're going
to Arrakis tomorrow.

127
00:10:59,835 --> 00:11:01,270
With the advance team.

128
00:11:01,370 --> 00:11:02,838
Yes, I'm going
to Arrakis tomorrow

129
00:11:02,905 --> 00:11:04,173
with the advance team.

130
00:11:05,340 --> 00:11:07,109
I'd like you
to take me with you.

131
00:11:07,743 --> 00:11:08,744
You would?

132
00:11:09,945 --> 00:11:11,680
Well, that's too bad.
'Cause no.

133
00:11:12,948 --> 00:11:14,183
[Paul] Duncan.

134
00:11:14,249 --> 00:11:16,518
Are you trying
to get me court-martialed?

135
00:11:17,586 --> 00:11:18,687
What's going on?

136
00:11:18,754 --> 00:11:20,189
Can I trust you
with something?

137
00:11:20,255 --> 00:11:21,523
Always. You know that.

138
00:11:23,559 --> 00:11:24,727
[sighs]

139
00:11:28,130 --> 00:11:29,898
I've been having dreams.

140
00:11:32,234 --> 00:11:34,970
About Arrakis and the Fremen.

141
00:11:35,070 --> 00:11:36,939
[ethereal music playing]

142
00:11:43,245 --> 00:11:44,980
[Duncan] Okay.

143
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:46,281
So?

144
00:11:47,750 --> 00:11:48,917
I saw you.

145
00:11:52,254 --> 00:11:54,323
With the Fremen.

146
00:11:54,423 --> 00:11:56,158
Ah.

147
00:11:56,258 --> 00:11:57,659
So, I do find them.

148
00:11:57,760 --> 00:12:00,095
There you go. That's a good
omen right there, right?

149
00:12:02,664 --> 00:12:03,665
Lanville!

150
00:12:10,105 --> 00:12:11,974
I saw you lying dead.

151
00:12:12,908 --> 00:12:14,676
Fallen in battle.

152
00:12:15,978 --> 00:12:18,313
It felt like
if I had been there,

153
00:12:18,413 --> 00:12:20,182
you'd be alive.

154
00:12:24,787 --> 00:12:26,655
First off, I'm not gonna die.

155
00:12:26,755 --> 00:12:27,923
You're not
taking me seriously.

156
00:12:27,990 --> 00:12:30,025
That's why
you want to come with me.

157
00:12:30,125 --> 00:12:31,460
Listen.

158
00:12:31,527 --> 00:12:33,195
Dreams make good stories,

159
00:12:33,295 --> 00:12:35,697
but everything important
happens when we're awake.

160
00:12:35,798 --> 00:12:37,866
'Cause that's when
we make things happen.

161
00:12:37,966 --> 00:12:40,302
Look at you.
Put on some muscle?

162
00:12:40,369 --> 00:12:41,603
I did?

163
00:12:41,670 --> 00:12:42,938
No.

164
00:12:45,207 --> 00:12:47,109
Hey.

165
00:12:47,176 --> 00:12:49,344
See you on Arrakis, my boy.

166
00:12:51,814 --> 00:12:53,115
[sighs]

167
00:12:56,618 --> 00:12:58,153
[animal chirping]

168
00:13:24,680 --> 00:13:26,748
Father, I'd like to ask
to join Duncan Idaho

169
00:13:26,849 --> 00:13:29,585
on his scout mission
to Arrakis tomorrow.

170
00:13:29,685 --> 00:13:31,587
I've studied the Fremen
language, I'd be an asset.

171
00:13:31,687 --> 00:13:32,921
Out of the question.

172
00:13:33,021 --> 00:13:34,323
You'll travel
in a few weeks to Arrakis,

173
00:13:34,389 --> 00:13:35,524
like the rest of us.

174
00:13:35,591 --> 00:13:36,892
I've been training
my whole life.

175
00:13:36,992 --> 00:13:38,227
What is the point

176
00:13:38,327 --> 00:13:39,595
if I'm not allowed
to face some actual risk?

177
00:13:39,695 --> 00:13:40,929
You know why, Paul.

178
00:13:41,029 --> 00:13:43,098
You're the future
of House Atreides.

179
00:13:43,198 --> 00:13:45,601
And Grandfather
fought bulls for sport!

180
00:13:45,701 --> 00:13:47,402
Yes.

181
00:13:47,502 --> 00:13:49,104
And look where that got him.

182
00:13:53,408 --> 00:13:55,777
I need you by my side.

183
00:13:55,878 --> 00:13:58,914
When we get to Arrakis,
we'll face enormous danger.

184
00:13:59,014 --> 00:14:00,549
What danger?

185
00:14:00,616 --> 00:14:02,517
The Fremen? The desert?

186
00:14:02,584 --> 00:14:04,553
Political danger.

187
00:14:06,555 --> 00:14:09,691
The Great Houses
look to us for leadership,

188
00:14:09,758 --> 00:14:11,793
and this threatens
the Emperor.

189
00:14:11,894 --> 00:14:15,130
By taking Arrakis from the
Harkonnens and making it ours,

190
00:14:15,230 --> 00:14:17,299
he sets the stage for a war

191
00:14:17,399 --> 00:14:19,534
which would weaken
both houses.

192
00:14:21,069 --> 00:14:22,804
But if we hold firm,

193
00:14:22,905 --> 00:14:24,973
and tap the true power
of Arrakis,

194
00:14:25,073 --> 00:14:27,376
we could be stronger
than ever.

195
00:14:27,442 --> 00:14:29,077
What does that mean?

196
00:14:29,144 --> 00:14:30,279
Mining spice,

197
00:14:30,379 --> 00:14:31,880
keeping the Fremen
in their place?

198
00:14:31,947 --> 00:14:33,148
We'd be no better
than Harkonnens.

199
00:14:33,248 --> 00:14:34,650
No.

200
00:14:34,750 --> 00:14:37,886
By making an alliance
with the Fremen.

201
00:14:37,953 --> 00:14:40,656
That's what I've sent
Duncan Idaho to arrange.

202
00:14:42,124 --> 00:14:43,258
Here on Caladan,

203
00:14:43,325 --> 00:14:45,827
we've ruled by air power
and sea power.

204
00:14:45,928 --> 00:14:49,765
On Arrakis, we need
to cultivate desert power.

205
00:14:53,001 --> 00:14:54,803
I want you sitting in
on my Council.

206
00:14:54,903 --> 00:14:56,271
Learn what I do.

207
00:14:56,338 --> 00:14:58,106
What if I'm not, Dad?

208
00:14:59,741 --> 00:15:01,143
Not what?

209
00:15:02,611 --> 00:15:05,180
The future of House Atreides.

210
00:15:07,649 --> 00:15:09,017
[Leto sighs]

211
00:15:17,459 --> 00:15:19,995
I told my father
I didn't want this either.

212
00:15:23,799 --> 00:15:25,801
I wanted to be a pilot.

213
00:15:27,135 --> 00:15:28,437
You never told me that.

214
00:15:31,473 --> 00:15:33,542
Your grandfather said,

215
00:15:33,642 --> 00:15:36,378
"A great man
doesn't seek to lead.

216
00:15:36,478 --> 00:15:40,115
He's called to it,
and he answers."

217
00:15:41,783 --> 00:15:43,685
And if your answer is no...

218
00:15:46,788 --> 00:15:49,992
you'll still be the only thing
I ever needed you to be...

219
00:15:51,827 --> 00:15:53,061
my son.

220
00:16:03,205 --> 00:16:07,175
I found my own way to it.
Maybe you'll find yours.

221
00:16:10,679 --> 00:16:12,514
In their memory...

222
00:16:15,050 --> 00:16:16,852
give it a try.

223
00:16:23,692 --> 00:16:25,560
[grunting]

224
00:16:25,660 --> 00:16:27,863
[Gurney] Don't stand
with your back to the door.

225
00:16:29,064 --> 00:16:30,599
How many times
do we have to tell you?

226
00:16:30,699 --> 00:16:32,100
[Paul grunts]
I could tell it was you

227
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:33,935
by your footsteps,
Gurney Halleck.

228
00:16:34,036 --> 00:16:36,772
[Gurney] Someone
might imitate my stride.

229
00:16:36,872 --> 00:16:38,106
[Paul] I know the difference.

230
00:16:38,206 --> 00:16:39,775
Are you the new
Weapons Master?

231
00:16:39,875 --> 00:16:43,612
With Duncan Idaho gone,
I must make do as best I can.

232
00:16:44,746 --> 00:16:46,114
Choose your blade.

233
00:16:46,214 --> 00:16:47,949
I've had quite a day, Gurney.

234
00:16:48,050 --> 00:16:50,085
Give us a song instead.

235
00:16:54,689 --> 00:16:55,757
[smacks lips] That's rude.

236
00:16:57,059 --> 00:16:58,360
[Paul grunts]

237
00:17:00,762 --> 00:17:02,397
[powers up]

238
00:17:05,534 --> 00:17:06,802
[device beeps]

239
00:17:10,572 --> 00:17:11,640
[Paul groans]

240
00:17:11,740 --> 00:17:13,208
[panting]

241
00:17:13,275 --> 00:17:14,810
[Gurney] Come on.

242
00:17:14,910 --> 00:17:15,911
Come on.

243
00:17:15,977 --> 00:17:17,212
Old man.

244
00:17:17,279 --> 00:17:18,447
[exhales forcefully]

245
00:17:24,553 --> 00:17:25,587
[Paul grunts]

246
00:17:27,089 --> 00:17:28,790
[device beeps]

247
00:17:28,890 --> 00:17:31,426
Ah, the slow blade
penetrates the shield.

248
00:17:36,264 --> 00:17:37,232
[groans]

249
00:17:38,500 --> 00:17:40,335
I guess I'm not
in the mood today.

250
00:17:40,435 --> 00:17:41,636
-Mood?
-Yeah.

251
00:17:41,736 --> 00:17:42,838
What's mood to do with it?

252
00:17:42,938 --> 00:17:44,673
You fight
when the necessity arises,

253
00:17:44,773 --> 00:17:45,774
no matter the mood.

254
00:17:45,841 --> 00:17:46,942
Now fight!

255
00:17:48,610 --> 00:17:50,445
[both grunting]

256
00:17:52,447 --> 00:17:53,448
Come on!

257
00:18:05,127 --> 00:18:07,496
-[device beeps]
-I have you.

258
00:18:07,596 --> 00:18:09,297
Aye.

259
00:18:09,364 --> 00:18:11,032
But look down, my lord.

260
00:18:11,133 --> 00:18:13,702
You'd have joined me in death.

261
00:18:13,802 --> 00:18:15,670
I see you found the mood.

262
00:18:16,938 --> 00:18:18,306
[Gurney panting]

263
00:18:22,711 --> 00:18:25,680
[devices deactivate]

264
00:18:27,883 --> 00:18:29,484
Will it be that bad?

265
00:18:29,551 --> 00:18:32,053
You don't get it, do you?

266
00:18:32,154 --> 00:18:33,388
You don't really understand

267
00:18:33,488 --> 00:18:36,158
the grave nature
of what's happening to us.

268
00:18:38,560 --> 00:18:40,061
For 80 years,

269
00:18:40,162 --> 00:18:42,297
Arrakis belonged
to House Harkonnen.

270
00:18:42,364 --> 00:18:44,866
80 years of owning
the spice fields.

271
00:18:44,966 --> 00:18:47,068
Can you imagine the wealth?

272
00:18:47,169 --> 00:18:49,070
Your eyes.
I need to see it in your eyes.

273
00:18:49,171 --> 00:18:51,673
You never met
Harkonnens before, I have.

274
00:18:51,740 --> 00:18:54,809
They're not human,
they're brutal!

275
00:18:54,876 --> 00:18:56,811
You have to be ready.

276
00:19:06,888 --> 00:19:09,024
[dramatic ominous music
playing]

277
00:19:38,720 --> 00:19:39,921
[Rabban] Lord Baron.

278
00:19:41,923 --> 00:19:44,125
[Vladimir] Rabban.

279
00:19:44,226 --> 00:19:46,895
The last of our ships
have left Arrakis.

280
00:19:47,762 --> 00:19:49,264
It's done.

281
00:19:49,364 --> 00:19:50,865
[Vladimir] Very good.

282
00:19:53,868 --> 00:19:55,937
Uncle, how can we
let this happen?

283
00:19:56,037 --> 00:19:58,073
How can the Emperor

284
00:19:58,139 --> 00:20:00,709
[shouting]
take everything we've built

285
00:20:00,775 --> 00:20:03,078
and give it to that Duke?

286
00:20:03,144 --> 00:20:04,446
How?

287
00:20:04,546 --> 00:20:07,449
Don't be too sure
it's an act of love.

288
00:20:07,549 --> 00:20:09,584
[breathes heavily]

289
00:20:09,651 --> 00:20:11,319
What does he mean?

290
00:20:16,925 --> 00:20:19,761
When is a gift not a gift?

291
00:20:21,496 --> 00:20:25,066
The Atreides' voice is rising,

292
00:20:25,133 --> 00:20:28,436
and the Emperor
is a jealous man.

293
00:20:30,605 --> 00:20:33,675
A dangerous, jealous man.

294
00:20:34,976 --> 00:20:36,778
[ominous music playing]

295
00:20:47,956 --> 00:20:50,025
[voices chanting indistinctly]

296
00:21:01,436 --> 00:21:03,505
[voices continue chanting]

297
00:21:32,167 --> 00:21:33,368
[voices fade]

298
00:21:45,347 --> 00:21:46,381
Paul.

299
00:21:47,882 --> 00:21:49,584
[softly] Paul, wake up.

300
00:21:55,390 --> 00:21:56,424
What's wrong?

301
00:21:56,524 --> 00:21:58,827
Get dressed and come with me.

302
00:22:19,247 --> 00:22:20,615
What is this?

303
00:22:20,715 --> 00:22:23,618
The Reverend Mother
Gaius Helen Mohiam is here.

304
00:22:23,718 --> 00:22:25,854
She was my teacher
at the Bene Gesserit school.

305
00:22:25,920 --> 00:22:29,457
She's now Truthsayer
to the Emperor himself.

306
00:22:29,557 --> 00:22:31,426
She would like to meet you.

307
00:22:32,026 --> 00:22:33,628
Why?

308
00:22:33,728 --> 00:22:36,064
She wants to know
about your dreams.

309
00:22:37,432 --> 00:22:39,267
How does she know
about my dreams?

310
00:22:41,936 --> 00:22:43,471
And why is Dr. Yueh here?

311
00:22:43,571 --> 00:22:45,940
He only needs a moment.

312
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:48,042
[Dr. Yueh] Hello, young master.

313
00:22:48,109 --> 00:22:50,812
Your mother asked me
to check your vitals.

314
00:22:56,785 --> 00:22:58,119
What's happening?

315
00:23:01,289 --> 00:23:03,391
[whispering in Mandarin]

316
00:23:19,607 --> 00:23:22,477
[in English] His heart
is strong as ever, my lady.

317
00:23:24,446 --> 00:23:25,680
[in sign language]

318
00:23:36,591 --> 00:23:37,692
Paul...

319
00:23:42,297 --> 00:23:43,765
[in sign language]

320
00:24:05,820 --> 00:24:11,326
[eerie voices]  Who are you?

321
00:24:15,697 --> 00:24:17,966
Defiance in the eyes.

322
00:24:18,032 --> 00:24:19,701
Like his father.

323
00:24:19,801 --> 00:24:21,369
Leave us.

324
00:24:21,469 --> 00:24:22,470
[whispers]
You must do everything

325
00:24:22,537 --> 00:24:23,905
the Reverend Mother tells you.

326
00:24:27,542 --> 00:24:28,877
You dismiss my mother
in her own house.

327
00:24:28,977 --> 00:24:30,144
[Mohiam in distorted voice]
Come here.

328
00:24:30,812 --> 00:24:31,813
Kneel.

329
00:24:35,917 --> 00:24:37,852
How dare you use
the Voice on me?

330
00:24:45,193 --> 00:24:46,494
[in normal voice] Put
your right hand in the box.

331
00:24:48,663 --> 00:24:51,065
Your mother bade you obey me.

332
00:24:51,165 --> 00:24:52,901
[Paul breathes heavily]

333
00:24:59,173 --> 00:25:01,609
I hold at your neck
the Gom Jabbar.

334
00:25:02,677 --> 00:25:04,345
A poison needle.

335
00:25:04,412 --> 00:25:05,713
Instant death.

336
00:25:06,748 --> 00:25:08,283
The test is simple.

337
00:25:08,383 --> 00:25:10,919
Remove your hand from the box

338
00:25:11,019 --> 00:25:12,587
and you die.

339
00:25:13,555 --> 00:25:15,290
What's in the box?

340
00:25:16,558 --> 00:25:17,625
Pain.

341
00:25:19,227 --> 00:25:22,430
-[scoffs]
-No need to call the guards.

342
00:25:22,530 --> 00:25:24,132
Your mother stands
behind that door.

343
00:25:24,232 --> 00:25:25,934
No one would get past her.

344
00:25:32,907 --> 00:25:34,409
[Paul]
Why are you doing this?

345
00:25:36,144 --> 00:25:37,478
An animal caught in a trap

346
00:25:37,579 --> 00:25:40,381
will gnaw off
its own leg to escape.

347
00:25:41,082 --> 00:25:42,383
What will you do?

348
00:25:47,956 --> 00:25:49,657
[high-pitched whirring]

349
00:25:54,896 --> 00:25:56,064
[groans]

350
00:25:59,934 --> 00:26:01,102
[exhales sharply]

351
00:26:05,106 --> 00:26:06,808
[sobbing softly]

352
00:26:07,976 --> 00:26:09,310
[shudders]

353
00:26:14,282 --> 00:26:16,417
-[grunts in pain]
-Silence.

354
00:26:16,484 --> 00:26:18,186
[Paul breathing raggedly]

355
00:26:23,358 --> 00:26:25,159
-[Paul grunts in pain]
-[shuddering]

356
00:26:25,259 --> 00:26:27,095
I must not fear.

357
00:26:28,830 --> 00:26:30,431
I must not fear.

358
00:26:31,699 --> 00:26:34,102
[stifles grunt, whimpers]

359
00:26:34,168 --> 00:26:36,771
[suppressed groan]

360
00:26:36,838 --> 00:26:38,706
Fear is the mind-killer.

361
00:26:40,808 --> 00:26:42,043
Fear

362
00:26:42,143 --> 00:26:44,512
is the little death
that brings obliteration.

363
00:26:44,612 --> 00:26:47,215
-[whirring intensifies]
-[Paul grunts]

364
00:26:47,315 --> 00:26:49,050
And I'll face my fear
and I'll permit it

365
00:26:49,150 --> 00:26:50,284
to pass over me
and through me.

366
00:26:57,492 --> 00:26:59,560
[ominous music playing]

367
00:27:00,662 --> 00:27:03,231
[dramatic lamentation music
playing]

368
00:27:03,331 --> 00:27:05,566
[searing]

369
00:27:05,667 --> 00:27:07,001
And when it has gone past...

370
00:27:15,677 --> 00:27:18,546
I will turn the inner eye
and see its path. [gasps]

371
00:27:21,582 --> 00:27:24,318
[sobs] And where the fear
has gone,

372
00:27:25,153 --> 00:27:26,187
there will be nothing.

373
00:27:31,192 --> 00:27:32,694
Only I will remain.

374
00:27:37,031 --> 00:27:38,232
Enough.

375
00:27:38,332 --> 00:27:40,535
-[panting]
-[whirring fading]

376
00:27:54,849 --> 00:27:57,452
Like sifting sand
through a screen,

377
00:27:57,552 --> 00:28:00,121
we sift people.

378
00:28:00,221 --> 00:28:03,091
If you had been unable
to control your impulses,

379
00:28:03,191 --> 00:28:04,759
like an animal,

380
00:28:04,859 --> 00:28:07,061
we could not let you live.

381
00:28:07,128 --> 00:28:09,797
You inherit too much power.

382
00:28:09,897 --> 00:28:11,032
What, because
I'm a duke's son?

383
00:28:11,099 --> 00:28:13,901
Because you are Jessica's son.

384
00:28:13,968 --> 00:28:16,604
You have more
than one birthright, boy.

385
00:28:18,239 --> 00:28:19,273
Jessica?

386
00:28:26,314 --> 00:28:28,649
You've been training him
in the Way.

387
00:28:33,087 --> 00:28:35,757
Tell me about these dreams.

388
00:28:35,823 --> 00:28:37,959
-I had one tonight.
-What did you see?

389
00:28:40,895 --> 00:28:42,263
A girl.

390
00:28:42,330 --> 00:28:43,998
On Arrakis.

391
00:28:44,098 --> 00:28:45,466
Have you dreamt of her before?

392
00:28:49,604 --> 00:28:50,905
Many times.

393
00:28:53,608 --> 00:28:55,643
Do you often dream
things that happen

394
00:28:55,743 --> 00:28:56,911
just as you dreamed them?

395
00:29:00,314 --> 00:29:01,616
Not exactly.

396
00:29:05,253 --> 00:29:06,854
Goodbye, young human.

397
00:29:07,655 --> 00:29:09,290
I hope you live.

398
00:29:17,131 --> 00:29:19,200
[Lady Jessica]
Did you have to go that far?

399
00:29:19,300 --> 00:29:21,035
[Mohiam] You chose
to train him in the Way,

400
00:29:21,135 --> 00:29:23,037
in defiance of our rule.

401
00:29:23,137 --> 00:29:24,672
He wields our power.

402
00:29:24,772 --> 00:29:27,542
He had to be
tested to the limits.

403
00:29:27,642 --> 00:29:30,878
So much potential,
wasted in a male.

404
00:29:30,978 --> 00:29:32,947
You were told
to bear only daughters.

405
00:29:33,014 --> 00:29:34,382
But you, in your pride,

406
00:29:34,482 --> 00:29:36,384
thought you could
produce the  Kwisatz Haderach.

407
00:29:36,484 --> 00:29:37,885
Was I wrong?

408
00:29:37,985 --> 00:29:40,721
You're lucky he didn't die
in that room.

409
00:29:40,822 --> 00:29:43,057
If he is The One,
he has a long way to go.

410
00:29:43,157 --> 00:29:46,194
His Sight is barely awakened,
and now he goes into the fire.

411
00:29:47,662 --> 00:29:50,131
But our plans
are measured in centuries.

412
00:29:50,198 --> 00:29:51,732
We have other prospects

413
00:29:51,833 --> 00:29:54,202
if he fails his promise.

414
00:29:56,804 --> 00:29:59,307
Do you see so little hope?

415
00:29:59,373 --> 00:30:00,741
[Mohiam] On Arrakis,
we have done

416
00:30:00,842 --> 00:30:02,476
all we can for you.

417
00:30:02,543 --> 00:30:04,378
A path has been laid.

418
00:30:04,478 --> 00:30:06,714
Let's hope
he doesn't squander it.

419
00:30:13,588 --> 00:30:15,723
[voices murmuring
indistinctly]

420
00:30:48,089 --> 00:30:49,790
[breathes heavily]

421
00:30:53,961 --> 00:30:55,296
[Lady Jessica] Paul.

422
00:30:56,197 --> 00:30:57,765
[Paul] What does it mean?

423
00:30:59,133 --> 00:31:00,801
That I could be The One?

424
00:31:00,902 --> 00:31:02,236
[Lady Jessica] You heard.

425
00:31:05,606 --> 00:31:06,874
The Bene Gesserit serve

426
00:31:06,941 --> 00:31:09,443
as powerful partners
to the Great Houses,

427
00:31:10,478 --> 00:31:11,746
but there's more to it.

428
00:31:11,812 --> 00:31:14,382
You steer the politics
of the Imperium

429
00:31:14,448 --> 00:31:15,883
from the shadows.

430
00:31:16,584 --> 00:31:17,585
I know.

431
00:31:17,652 --> 00:31:20,121
You don't know everything.

432
00:31:20,221 --> 00:31:22,490
For thousands of years,

433
00:31:22,590 --> 00:31:25,226
we've been carefully
crossings bloodlines

434
00:31:25,293 --> 00:31:27,428
-to bring forth...
-The One?

435
00:31:28,596 --> 00:31:30,064
A mind...

436
00:31:31,799 --> 00:31:36,137
powerful enough
to bridge space and time.

437
00:31:36,938 --> 00:31:38,773
Past and future.

438
00:31:40,775 --> 00:31:43,077
Who can help us
into a better future.

439
00:31:44,278 --> 00:31:46,948
We think he's very close now.

440
00:31:48,916 --> 00:31:51,085
Some believe he's here.

441
00:31:55,089 --> 00:31:57,091
All part of a plan.

442
00:32:13,841 --> 00:32:15,977
[slow dramatic music playing]

443
00:32:51,345 --> 00:32:53,514
[slow dramatic music
continues]

444
00:34:12,059 --> 00:34:13,561
[spaceship lands]

445
00:34:15,229 --> 00:34:16,230
Shield.

446
00:34:27,274 --> 00:34:28,776
[metallic groan]

447
00:34:31,445 --> 00:34:32,746
[metallic thudding]

448
00:34:33,781 --> 00:34:34,915
[door opens]

449
00:34:58,672 --> 00:35:00,541
"My lungs taste
the air of Time,

450
00:35:00,641 --> 00:35:02,643
Blown past falling sand..."

451
00:35:02,710 --> 00:35:04,345
[bagpipe playing]

452
00:35:14,355 --> 00:35:16,490
[band playing
patriotic music]

453
00:35:47,321 --> 00:35:48,422
Thufir Hawat.

454
00:35:52,927 --> 00:35:54,395
Young master!

455
00:35:54,495 --> 00:35:56,764
How does it feel
to walk on a new world?

456
00:35:56,864 --> 00:35:58,766
Exciting, to say the least.

457
00:35:59,500 --> 00:36:01,335
My lord.

458
00:36:01,402 --> 00:36:03,037
How are you, old friend?

459
00:36:03,103 --> 00:36:05,439
My advance team
has secured the city.

460
00:36:05,539 --> 00:36:08,542
We're still smoothing out
a few rough spots.

461
00:36:10,177 --> 00:36:11,512
My lady.

462
00:36:15,950 --> 00:36:17,918
[woman]  Lisan al-Gaib!

463
00:36:30,064 --> 00:36:31,799
[crowd clamoring]

464
00:36:33,701 --> 00:36:36,704
[man]  Lisan al-Gaib!
Lisan al-Gaib!

465
00:36:37,771 --> 00:36:39,773
[woman 2]  Lisan al-Gaib!

466
00:36:39,873 --> 00:36:42,109
[crowd chanting]
Lisan al-Gaib! Lisan al-Gaib!

467
00:36:42,209 --> 00:36:45,145
Lisan al-Gaib! Lisan al-Gaib!

468
00:36:45,246 --> 00:36:48,148
Lisan al-Gaib! Lisan al-Gaib!

469
00:36:48,249 --> 00:36:51,252
Lisan al-Gaib! Lisan al-Gaib!

470
00:36:52,953 --> 00:36:54,722
Don't be fooled
by the welcome.

471
00:36:54,788 --> 00:36:56,657
They follow
their old masters' rules.

472
00:36:56,757 --> 00:36:57,891
Mandatory attendance.

473
00:36:57,958 --> 00:37:00,261
That's Harkonnen love
out there.

474
00:37:01,262 --> 00:37:03,330
[crowd continues chanting]

475
00:37:06,934 --> 00:37:08,335
Atreides!

476
00:37:08,435 --> 00:37:12,006
[soldiers chanting]
Atreides! Atreides! Atreides!

477
00:37:12,106 --> 00:37:15,843
Atreides! Atreides! Atreides!

478
00:37:15,943 --> 00:37:18,412
Atreides! Atreides!

479
00:37:20,514 --> 00:37:23,284
[Thufir] Let's get you
out of the sun.

480
00:37:23,350 --> 00:37:25,853
The heat can kill
in this place.

481
00:37:35,095 --> 00:37:37,364
[ornithopters powering up]

482
00:37:42,102 --> 00:37:43,837
They were pointing at us.

483
00:37:44,838 --> 00:37:46,173
What are they shouting?

484
00:37:46,273 --> 00:37:50,177
Lisan al-Gaib.
"Voice from the Outer World."

485
00:37:50,277 --> 00:37:52,980
It's their name for "messiah."

486
00:37:53,047 --> 00:37:56,350
It means the Bene Gesserit
have been at work here.

487
00:37:56,450 --> 00:37:58,886
Planting superstitions.

488
00:37:58,986 --> 00:38:01,789
Preparing the way, Paul.

489
00:38:01,855 --> 00:38:04,191
These people
have waited for centuries

490
00:38:04,291 --> 00:38:06,026
for the  Lisan al-Gaib.

491
00:38:06,727 --> 00:38:07,828
They see you,

492
00:38:08,662 --> 00:38:10,564
they see the signs.

493
00:38:13,167 --> 00:38:15,636
They see
what they've been told to see.

494
00:38:20,708 --> 00:38:21,742
We're good to go.

495
00:39:05,252 --> 00:39:06,587
[Thufir] Shield Wall.

496
00:39:06,687 --> 00:39:08,555
Protects the city
from the weather

497
00:39:08,622 --> 00:39:10,124
and the worms.

498
00:39:18,899 --> 00:39:21,201
[eerie dramatic music playing]

499
00:39:56,970 --> 00:39:59,807
[Gurney] The locals call
the big one the Hand of God.

500
00:40:01,608 --> 00:40:04,178
[Leto] Well, the Hand of God
is wreaking havoc

501
00:40:04,278 --> 00:40:05,813
on our comms system.

502
00:40:09,016 --> 00:40:10,484
It's so quiet.

503
00:40:11,518 --> 00:40:13,587
[Gurney] Yeah.

504
00:40:13,654 --> 00:40:15,522
That's what worries me, too.

505
00:40:22,296 --> 00:40:24,031
[Leto] There's the spaceport

506
00:40:24,131 --> 00:40:26,767
and that plume of dust there
is the spice refinery.

507
00:40:26,834 --> 00:40:28,936
Our two
most vulnerable points.

508
00:40:29,002 --> 00:40:30,304
I want you guarding them.

509
00:40:30,370 --> 00:40:33,006
If we can't refine spice
and ship it off-world,

510
00:40:33,106 --> 00:40:35,142
-we're dead here.
-[Lanville] My lord.

511
00:40:35,209 --> 00:40:37,845
The sun's getting too high.
We need to seal the doors.

512
00:40:40,848 --> 00:40:42,049
[Leto sighs]

513
00:40:42,149 --> 00:40:44,718
What do they say
about this hellhole again?

514
00:40:44,818 --> 00:40:47,287
"To shower, you scrub your ass
with sand," my lord.

515
00:40:47,354 --> 00:40:48,889
That's what they say.

516
00:40:48,989 --> 00:40:50,624
That's what they say.

517
00:40:55,162 --> 00:40:57,865
[Thufir] Candidates
for a housekeeper, my lady.

518
00:41:13,647 --> 00:41:15,148
What is your name?

519
00:41:15,215 --> 00:41:17,384
Shadout Mapes, my lady.

520
00:41:19,152 --> 00:41:21,221
[Lady Jessica]
The rest of you may go.

521
00:41:21,321 --> 00:41:22,422
Thank you.

522
00:41:24,725 --> 00:41:26,693
Shadout.

523
00:41:26,760 --> 00:41:28,562
It's an old Chakobsa word.

524
00:41:29,329 --> 00:41:30,764
"Well-dipper."

525
00:41:32,366 --> 00:41:33,667
[speaking Chakobsa]

526
00:41:33,734 --> 00:41:34,935
[in English]
You know the ancient tongues?

527
00:41:35,035 --> 00:41:36,503
I know many things.

528
00:41:36,570 --> 00:41:39,740
I know that you have a weapon
concealed in your bodice.

529
00:41:40,707 --> 00:41:41,875
[in sign language]

530
00:41:41,942 --> 00:41:43,510
[speaking]
If you mean to harm me,

531
00:41:43,577 --> 00:41:46,079
I must warn you,
whatever you're hiding,

532
00:41:46,914 --> 00:41:48,682
it won't be enough.

533
00:41:50,417 --> 00:41:52,920
The weapon is meant as a gift

534
00:41:53,854 --> 00:41:56,056
if you are truly The One.

535
00:42:11,872 --> 00:42:13,473
Do you know this?

536
00:42:14,808 --> 00:42:16,443
It's a crysknife.

537
00:42:20,247 --> 00:42:21,648
Do you know its meaning?

538
00:42:22,583 --> 00:42:24,418
[in sign language]

539
00:42:25,886 --> 00:42:27,487
It's a maker...

540
00:42:27,588 --> 00:42:29,389
[wailing]

541
00:42:32,593 --> 00:42:35,062
A maker of the deep desert.

542
00:42:37,598 --> 00:42:40,000
When you have lived
with prophecy for so long,

543
00:42:40,100 --> 00:42:42,669
the moment of revelation
is a shock.

544
00:42:42,769 --> 00:42:44,438
Lisan al-Gaib.

545
00:42:44,504 --> 00:42:46,640
The mother and the son.

546
00:42:52,579 --> 00:42:54,314
It is yours.

547
00:42:55,916 --> 00:42:59,519
Tooth of  Shai-Hulud.

548
00:43:01,588 --> 00:43:03,924
[ancient meditation music
playing]

549
00:43:29,650 --> 00:43:32,452
[men chanting in distance]
Lisan! Lisan al-Gaib!

550
00:43:32,519 --> 00:43:36,657
Lisan al-Gaib! Lisan al-Gaib!

551
00:43:47,000 --> 00:43:48,201
[Paul] Hello.

552
00:43:50,570 --> 00:43:53,306
You shouldn't be out here
at this hour of the day.

553
00:43:55,475 --> 00:43:57,711
They're out here.

554
00:43:57,811 --> 00:44:00,414
[gardener] Hmm.
Fremen pilgrims.

555
00:44:00,514 --> 00:44:02,482
They don't care
about heatstroke.

556
00:44:04,184 --> 00:44:07,421
I didn't know date palms
could even be found out here.

557
00:44:07,521 --> 00:44:10,657
[gardener] Oh,
these aren't indigenous.

558
00:44:10,724 --> 00:44:13,193
They can't survive without me.

559
00:44:13,260 --> 00:44:14,494
Each one of these

560
00:44:14,561 --> 00:44:17,164
drinks every day
the equivalent of five men.

561
00:44:19,266 --> 00:44:20,934
Twenty palm trees.

562
00:44:22,235 --> 00:44:24,771
A hundred lives.

563
00:44:24,871 --> 00:44:26,907
Should we remove them?
Save the water?

564
00:44:27,007 --> 00:44:28,408
No, no, no.

565
00:44:28,508 --> 00:44:30,077
These are sacred.

566
00:44:34,448 --> 00:44:35,916
Old dream.

567
00:44:43,790 --> 00:44:45,959
[narrator over speakers]
The largest and most dangerous

568
00:44:46,059 --> 00:44:49,029
organism on Arrakis
is the sandworm,

569
00:44:49,096 --> 00:44:53,233
capable of reaching
400 meters in length.

570
00:44:53,300 --> 00:44:55,702
To avoid making
rhythmic noises,

571
00:44:55,769 --> 00:44:57,270
which attract the sandworms,

572
00:44:57,370 --> 00:45:01,308
the Fremen cross desert spaces
using the sandwalk,

573
00:45:01,408 --> 00:45:04,411
a dance-like motion
with irregular rhythm

574
00:45:04,478 --> 00:45:08,482
which emulates the natural
sounds of the desert.

575
00:45:08,582 --> 00:45:11,218
What scant plant life
exists on Arrakis

576
00:45:11,284 --> 00:45:12,886
is thanks to the Fremen,

577
00:45:12,953 --> 00:45:15,889
who have cultivated
deep-rooted terranic plants

578
00:45:15,956 --> 00:45:18,992
such as saguaro, burrobush,

579
00:45:19,092 --> 00:45:23,163
sand-verbena and incense bush.

580
00:45:23,263 --> 00:45:26,500
The shepherd's tree has
the deepest documented roots,

581
00:45:26,600 --> 00:45:31,104
stretching more than
450 feet deep.

582
00:45:31,171 --> 00:45:33,073
These plants cling to life

583
00:45:33,140 --> 00:45:36,443
in a parched,
nutrient-poor landscape.

584
00:45:49,923 --> 00:45:52,159
[slow suspenseful music
playing]

585
00:46:32,499 --> 00:46:34,568
[music building up]

586
00:46:41,074 --> 00:46:42,475
[both gasp]

587
00:46:46,580 --> 00:46:48,315
[Paul] It's a hunter-seeker.

588
00:46:48,381 --> 00:46:50,417
The operator must be nearby.

589
00:46:50,517 --> 00:46:52,719
[dramatic music playing]

590
00:46:55,488 --> 00:46:56,923
[Thufir]  The Harkonnen agent
was cemented

591
00:46:57,023 --> 00:46:58,892
into that hole six weeks ago.

592
00:46:58,992 --> 00:47:00,694
Ran the hunter-seeker
through a water pipe

593
00:47:00,760 --> 00:47:01,862
inside the walls.

594
00:47:03,163 --> 00:47:06,233
Sire, I failed you today.
There's no excuse.

595
00:47:06,333 --> 00:47:07,734
You have my resignation.

596
00:47:07,834 --> 00:47:09,102
You would deprive us
of your talents at this time?

597
00:47:09,202 --> 00:47:10,403
Sire, my honor demands...

598
00:47:10,503 --> 00:47:12,205
They tried to take
the life of my son!

599
00:47:13,373 --> 00:47:14,841
I don't give a damn
about your honor.

600
00:47:14,908 --> 00:47:17,510
You want absolution?
Go catch some spies.

601
00:47:17,577 --> 00:47:18,778
Your Grace.

602
00:47:26,086 --> 00:47:28,355
[Mohiam] The thing must leave.

603
00:47:28,421 --> 00:47:30,924
[man] You can speak
without fear.

604
00:47:31,024 --> 00:47:33,293
Our pet doesn't understand
your language.

605
00:47:33,393 --> 00:47:34,861
[Mohiam in distorted voice]
Get out.

606
00:47:39,232 --> 00:47:41,034
[normal voice] It understands.

607
00:47:41,101 --> 00:47:42,636
Activate silence.

608
00:47:47,307 --> 00:47:48,875
[low, muffled speech]

609
00:47:58,051 --> 00:48:00,553
[Mohiam] It must
never be known.

610
00:48:00,620 --> 00:48:03,556
[Vladimir] There's
no satellites over Arrakis.

611
00:48:03,623 --> 00:48:07,260
The Atreides
will die in the dark.

612
00:48:07,327 --> 00:48:08,995
[Mohiam] On that matter,

613
00:48:09,095 --> 00:48:12,265
Duke Leto Atreides
means nothing to our order.

614
00:48:12,332 --> 00:48:14,301
But his wife
is under our protection

615
00:48:14,401 --> 00:48:17,003
and by extension, her son.

616
00:48:17,103 --> 00:48:19,606
Allow them
the dignity of exile.

617
00:48:21,608 --> 00:48:23,677
[sighs]

618
00:48:23,777 --> 00:48:25,679
House Harkonnen
would never dream

619
00:48:25,779 --> 00:48:28,748
of violating
the sanctity of your order.

620
00:48:29,783 --> 00:48:31,451
I give you my word.

621
00:48:31,518 --> 00:48:33,186
We will not harm them.

622
00:48:53,440 --> 00:48:54,975
If the Duke's son lives...

623
00:48:55,041 --> 00:48:57,544
No Atreides will live.

624
00:48:57,644 --> 00:49:00,046
My lord, you gave your word
to the witch.

625
00:49:00,146 --> 00:49:01,214
She sees too much.

626
00:49:01,314 --> 00:49:03,049
I said I would not harm them.

627
00:49:03,149 --> 00:49:04,384
And I shall not.

628
00:49:04,484 --> 00:49:06,786
But Arrakis is Arrakis.

629
00:49:07,988 --> 00:49:10,557
And the desert takes the weak.

630
00:49:12,659 --> 00:49:13,893
My desert.

631
00:49:13,994 --> 00:49:16,062
[sinister music playing]

632
00:49:16,730 --> 00:49:18,698
My Arrakis.

633
00:49:20,633 --> 00:49:22,302
My Dune.

634
00:49:25,505 --> 00:49:27,841
[Gurney] Your first
strategy meeting.

635
00:49:27,907 --> 00:49:29,142
Paul Atreides,

636
00:49:29,209 --> 00:49:31,144
who catches hunter-seekers
in his bare hands

637
00:49:31,211 --> 00:49:32,345
like a hero of old.

638
00:49:32,412 --> 00:49:34,681
[laughter]

639
00:49:34,748 --> 00:49:36,916
[whispers] Thanks
for the humiliation, old man.

640
00:49:37,017 --> 00:49:38,318
Gotta keep an eye on you.

641
00:49:39,185 --> 00:49:40,487
Attention!

642
00:49:48,495 --> 00:49:49,863
Let's get started.

643
00:49:52,265 --> 00:49:54,100
Thufir. Operations.

644
00:49:54,200 --> 00:49:56,870
I secured a copy of
the Harkonnens' account books.

645
00:49:57,704 --> 00:49:59,239
[men murmuring]

646
00:49:59,339 --> 00:50:00,607
The Harkonnens were taking

647
00:50:00,707 --> 00:50:04,177
10 billion solaris
out of here every year.

648
00:50:04,244 --> 00:50:06,913
"They shall suck of
the abundance of the seas,

649
00:50:07,013 --> 00:50:08,515
and the treasure
hid in the sand."

650
00:50:08,581 --> 00:50:10,950
[Thufir] We won't see profits
like that for a while.

651
00:50:11,051 --> 00:50:13,219
Not with the equipment
they left us.

652
00:50:14,187 --> 00:50:15,789
How bad is it?

653
00:50:21,528 --> 00:50:23,530
[Thufir] These are spice silos.

654
00:50:24,898 --> 00:50:27,967
We're meant
to fill every crate.

655
00:50:28,068 --> 00:50:29,969
[Paul] All of them?

656
00:50:30,070 --> 00:50:32,906
Every 25 standard days.

657
00:50:32,972 --> 00:50:35,308
Harkonnen sabotage
slows us down.

658
00:50:35,408 --> 00:50:37,110
[Paul] But who's
meant to arbitrate?

659
00:50:37,210 --> 00:50:38,411
Isn't there
a Judge of the Change

660
00:50:38,478 --> 00:50:39,779
to oversee the transition?

661
00:50:39,879 --> 00:50:41,281
Who did the Emperor appoint?

662
00:50:41,381 --> 00:50:44,150
Dr. Liet Kynes.
Imperial Ecologist.

663
00:50:44,250 --> 00:50:45,752
Been here 20 years.

664
00:50:45,819 --> 00:50:47,654
Eccentric, from what I'm told.

665
00:50:47,754 --> 00:50:50,790
I want to see these
harvesting fields myself.

666
00:50:50,890 --> 00:50:52,258
I wouldn't recommend it,
my lord.

667
00:50:52,325 --> 00:50:54,794
Have this Judge of the Change
accompany us.

668
00:50:54,894 --> 00:50:56,329
A meeting's long overdue.

669
00:50:56,429 --> 00:50:58,631
And we'll get
a bit of Imperial protection.

670
00:50:58,731 --> 00:51:00,233
A hostage. [chuckles]

671
00:51:00,300 --> 00:51:01,601
I love it.

672
00:51:01,668 --> 00:51:02,769
Hmm.

673
00:51:02,836 --> 00:51:05,105
-[engine roaring]
-He's here, my lord.

674
00:51:27,327 --> 00:51:28,962
[Duncan well-wishing
in Chakobsa]

675
00:51:29,028 --> 00:51:30,997
[in English] Take care
of them. They are friends.

676
00:51:31,097 --> 00:51:32,031
[Paul] Duncan!

677
00:51:32,132 --> 00:51:33,500
[Duncan] Ah! My boy!

678
00:51:34,300 --> 00:51:36,769
[both laughing]

679
00:51:39,305 --> 00:51:40,473
I swear you're getting taller.

680
00:51:40,540 --> 00:51:42,208
[Paul] Well,
you smell much worse.

681
00:51:45,945 --> 00:51:47,881
For four weeks,
I lived with the Fremen.

682
00:51:47,981 --> 00:51:49,048
Hidden in the desert,

683
00:51:49,149 --> 00:51:50,850
in a community
called a  sietch.

684
00:51:50,950 --> 00:51:52,218
Stilgar, the leader
of that  sietch,

685
00:51:52,318 --> 00:51:54,120
has come with me
to meet you, sire.

686
00:51:54,187 --> 00:51:56,523
This  sietch,  how is it hidden?

687
00:51:56,623 --> 00:51:57,690
It's underground.

688
00:51:57,790 --> 00:51:59,726
Arrakis is filled
with caverns.

689
00:51:59,826 --> 00:52:01,494
How big was the place?

690
00:52:01,561 --> 00:52:04,030
I'd say 10,000 people.

691
00:52:04,130 --> 00:52:05,665
And there are
hundreds of  sietches.

692
00:52:06,866 --> 00:52:08,301
Millions of Fremen.

693
00:52:09,068 --> 00:52:10,537
You were right.

694
00:52:10,637 --> 00:52:13,973
The Harkonnen estimate was
50,000 on the whole planet.

695
00:52:14,040 --> 00:52:16,242
The Fremen watched me
search for them for days.

696
00:52:16,342 --> 00:52:17,810
I never saw them.

697
00:52:17,877 --> 00:52:20,580
Finally, they sent
a warrior out to kill me.

698
00:52:20,680 --> 00:52:22,248
And I gotta tell you,

699
00:52:22,348 --> 00:52:24,751
I have never come
so close to dying.

700
00:52:24,851 --> 00:52:27,654
There's no finer fighter
in the Imperium.

701
00:52:27,720 --> 00:52:29,322
They fight like demons.

702
00:52:29,389 --> 00:52:31,257
Desert power.

703
00:52:33,693 --> 00:52:35,428
Duncan.

704
00:52:35,528 --> 00:52:36,996
-Well done.
-Thank you, my lord.

705
00:52:37,063 --> 00:52:38,431
[man] Sire.

706
00:52:38,531 --> 00:52:41,100
Their leader has a knife
he won't surrender, sire.

707
00:52:41,201 --> 00:52:44,270
It's a crysknife.
It's sacred to his people.

708
00:52:44,370 --> 00:52:45,572
Let him pass.

709
00:53:02,222 --> 00:53:03,590
[Gurney] Stop there.

710
00:53:03,690 --> 00:53:05,358
Hey! Hey!

711
00:53:08,928 --> 00:53:09,929
Mm.

712
00:53:10,730 --> 00:53:11,931
[Leto] Stilgar.

713
00:53:12,899 --> 00:53:14,067
Welcome.

714
00:53:15,268 --> 00:53:17,637
Sir, I respect
the personal dignity

715
00:53:17,737 --> 00:53:19,539
of any man that respects mine.

716
00:53:21,074 --> 00:53:22,742
[inhales deeply]

717
00:53:22,809 --> 00:53:23,876
[Stilgar] Hmm.

718
00:53:25,278 --> 00:53:26,746
[inhales deeply]

719
00:53:27,413 --> 00:53:28,615
[Duncan] Hold.

720
00:53:29,882 --> 00:53:31,784
[clears throat]
Thank you, Stilgar,

721
00:53:31,884 --> 00:53:35,288
for the gift
of your body's moisture.

722
00:53:35,388 --> 00:53:37,724
We accept it in the spirit
in which it was given.

723
00:53:43,396 --> 00:53:44,564
[Leto snorts]

724
00:53:45,732 --> 00:53:46,799
[Leto] I'm glad you've come.

725
00:53:47,767 --> 00:53:49,669
I believe your people and mine

726
00:53:49,769 --> 00:53:51,070
have much
to offer one another.

727
00:53:51,137 --> 00:53:52,505
No, no, you are Outworlders.

728
00:53:52,605 --> 00:53:54,274
You come here for the spice,

729
00:53:54,340 --> 00:53:56,809
you take it,
giving nothing in return.

730
00:53:58,578 --> 00:53:59,612
That's true.

731
00:54:01,514 --> 00:54:04,450
I know you've suffered
at the hands of the Harkonnen.

732
00:54:05,618 --> 00:54:07,086
Name what you want.

733
00:54:07,153 --> 00:54:08,354
If it's in my power to grant,

734
00:54:08,454 --> 00:54:09,922
I'll give it
and ask for nothing.

735
00:54:09,989 --> 00:54:12,859
Mm. I ask for this.
Do not seek our  sietches.

736
00:54:12,959 --> 00:54:15,795
Do not trespass in our lands.

737
00:54:15,862 --> 00:54:19,332
The desert was ours
long before you came.

738
00:54:19,432 --> 00:54:21,200
So, come and dig your spice,

739
00:54:21,301 --> 00:54:22,502
but when you have it,

740
00:54:22,602 --> 00:54:24,704
go back to this side
of the Shield Wall

741
00:54:24,804 --> 00:54:26,606
and leave the desert
to the Fremen.

742
00:54:26,673 --> 00:54:29,475
You will address the Duke
as "my lord" or "sire."

743
00:54:29,542 --> 00:54:32,145
[Leto] Gurney, just...
Just a moment.

744
00:54:32,211 --> 00:54:33,546
The Emperor

745
00:54:33,646 --> 00:54:36,382
has given me Arrakis
as my fief

746
00:54:36,482 --> 00:54:38,217
to rule and protect.

747
00:54:38,318 --> 00:54:40,820
I cannot promise
not to travel into the desert

748
00:54:40,887 --> 00:54:43,723
if duty compels me.

749
00:54:43,823 --> 00:54:46,726
But your  sietches
will be yours forever.

750
00:54:46,826 --> 00:54:49,395
And you will never be hunted
while I govern here.

751
00:54:53,900 --> 00:54:55,735
That's very honorable.

752
00:54:55,835 --> 00:54:58,504
I must go. That's all
I have to say to you.

753
00:54:58,571 --> 00:55:00,740
[Paul] Won't you stay?

754
00:55:00,840 --> 00:55:02,208
We would honor you.

755
00:55:02,308 --> 00:55:05,378
Honor requires
that I be elsewhere.

756
00:55:07,347 --> 00:55:08,581
[speaking Chakobsa]

757
00:55:17,056 --> 00:55:18,324
I don't like him.

758
00:55:18,391 --> 00:55:20,660
Our plan bears fruit.

759
00:55:20,727 --> 00:55:22,161
But it will take time?

760
00:55:22,228 --> 00:55:23,496
Yes.

761
00:55:24,430 --> 00:55:26,733
It will take time.

762
00:55:29,502 --> 00:55:30,870
Here, this is for you.

763
00:55:34,941 --> 00:55:36,943
It's a paracompass.

764
00:55:37,043 --> 00:55:39,545
The moons here
have a magnetic field, so...

765
00:55:39,612 --> 00:55:42,248
a simple compass needle
won't point north.

766
00:55:42,348 --> 00:55:44,450
Takes a clever piece
of clockwork to sort it out.

767
00:55:44,550 --> 00:55:46,219
[Paul] The Fremen make these?

768
00:55:46,285 --> 00:55:48,121
And stillsuits,
and sand compactors,

769
00:55:48,221 --> 00:55:49,622
and all kinds
of ingenious things.

770
00:55:49,722 --> 00:55:51,691
[Gurney] What the hell
is a sand compactor?

771
00:55:53,893 --> 00:55:54,961
[Duncan]
That's a sand compactor.

772
00:55:55,061 --> 00:55:56,129
[all chuckle]

773
00:55:56,229 --> 00:55:58,965
My God, man,
you've gone native.

774
00:55:59,065 --> 00:56:00,366
You admire them.

775
00:56:01,634 --> 00:56:03,136
I do.

776
00:56:03,236 --> 00:56:05,905
They're fierce but loyal.

777
00:56:05,972 --> 00:56:07,774
They're attuned to the desert.

778
00:56:07,874 --> 00:56:09,108
Part of it.

779
00:56:09,208 --> 00:56:11,310
It's part of them.

780
00:56:11,411 --> 00:56:12,578
You wait till you see it.

781
00:56:13,413 --> 00:56:14,814
It's beautiful out there.

782
00:56:18,084 --> 00:56:20,119
[announcer]
Sunrise warning, all workers.

783
00:56:20,219 --> 00:56:23,156
Temperature today
will reach 140 degrees.

784
00:56:23,256 --> 00:56:24,991
We are currently 90 degrees,

785
00:56:25,091 --> 00:56:28,461
and in 10 minutes,
we will hit 120 degrees.

786
00:56:29,562 --> 00:56:30,830
Last warning call.

787
00:56:30,930 --> 00:56:32,965
[dramatic music playing]

788
00:56:44,911 --> 00:56:46,979
[dramatic music continues]

789
00:57:04,130 --> 00:57:06,299
The Judge of the Change, sire.

790
00:57:06,365 --> 00:57:08,334
Dr. Liet Kynes.

791
00:57:08,434 --> 00:57:09,836
My lord Duke.

792
00:57:10,636 --> 00:57:12,205
Welcome to Arrakis.

793
00:57:12,305 --> 00:57:14,373
[Paul] You're
the Imperial Ecologist.

794
00:57:14,474 --> 00:57:16,375
Thank you for the stillsuits.

795
00:57:16,476 --> 00:57:18,544
They are of Fremen make.

796
00:57:18,644 --> 00:57:19,712
The best.

797
00:57:19,812 --> 00:57:21,113
With your permission, sire,

798
00:57:21,180 --> 00:57:22,548
I must check
the integrity of your suit...

799
00:57:22,648 --> 00:57:23,783
[Leto] Whoa.

800
00:57:24,484 --> 00:57:25,685
It's all right.

801
00:57:27,320 --> 00:57:29,522
It's all right.

802
00:57:29,622 --> 00:57:33,192
[chuckles lightly] Dr. Kynes,
we're in your hands.

803
00:57:37,730 --> 00:57:38,898
A stillsuit

804
00:57:38,998 --> 00:57:42,969
is a high-efficiency
filtration system.

805
00:57:43,035 --> 00:57:44,637
Even this early
in the morning,

806
00:57:44,704 --> 00:57:47,507
you wouldn't survive two hours
without one of these.

807
00:57:48,407 --> 00:57:50,676
It cools the body

808
00:57:50,743 --> 00:57:54,580
and recycles
the water lost to sweat.

809
00:57:54,680 --> 00:57:57,984
Your body's movements
provide the power.

810
00:57:58,050 --> 00:57:59,752
Inside the mask,
you'll find a tube

811
00:57:59,852 --> 00:58:01,921
to allow you to drink
the recycled water.

812
00:58:02,021 --> 00:58:03,256
[Leto] Mm.

813
00:58:03,356 --> 00:58:04,690
In good working order,
your suit won't lose

814
00:58:04,757 --> 00:58:07,059
more than a thimbleful
of water a day.

815
00:58:07,159 --> 00:58:08,494
[Leto] Most impressive.

816
00:58:10,196 --> 00:58:11,531
Let's have a look at you, lad.

817
00:58:13,866 --> 00:58:15,268
You've...

818
00:58:15,368 --> 00:58:16,569
worn a stillsuit before?

819
00:58:16,669 --> 00:58:18,271
No, this is my first time.

820
00:58:20,506 --> 00:58:23,109
Your desert boots are fitted
slip-fashion at the ankles.

821
00:58:23,209 --> 00:58:25,044
Who taught you to do that?

822
00:58:25,111 --> 00:58:27,179
It seemed the right way.

823
00:58:30,049 --> 00:58:31,551
[speaking Chakobsa]

824
00:58:34,887 --> 00:58:35,955
[in English] Are you Fremen?

825
00:58:37,723 --> 00:58:41,627
I am accepted
in both  sietch  and village.

826
00:58:41,727 --> 00:58:44,397
Now, come and see
the spice sands

827
00:58:44,463 --> 00:58:47,533
on which
your livelihood depends.

828
00:58:52,538 --> 00:58:54,574
[dramatic music playing]

829
00:59:25,471 --> 00:59:26,672
What would you do

830
00:59:26,772 --> 00:59:28,307
if your ornithopter
went down out here?

831
00:59:28,407 --> 00:59:30,509
You wouldn't want
to go down out there.

832
00:59:30,610 --> 00:59:32,178
It's worm territory.

833
00:59:34,814 --> 00:59:35,915
Dust cloud.

834
00:59:36,983 --> 00:59:39,185
[Leto] I see it.

835
00:59:39,285 --> 00:59:41,420
That's one of your harvesters.

836
00:59:44,090 --> 00:59:46,158
[dramatic music continues]

837
00:59:59,472 --> 01:00:01,641
[machinery clunking]

838
01:00:07,346 --> 01:00:08,514
[Dr. Kynes]
You can see the spice

839
01:00:08,614 --> 01:00:10,483
scattered over the surface.

840
01:00:11,984 --> 01:00:13,986
A rich spice bed

841
01:00:14,053 --> 01:00:15,521
by the color.

842
01:00:15,621 --> 01:00:18,124
If you get a little higher,
you'll have a better view.

843
01:00:32,838 --> 01:00:35,474
You see these spotter aircraft
looking for wormsign.

844
01:00:37,510 --> 01:00:38,711
[Paul] Wormsign?

845
01:00:38,811 --> 01:00:41,080
A sand wave
moving toward the crawler.

846
01:00:41,180 --> 01:00:43,382
Worms travel deep
but get closer

847
01:00:43,482 --> 01:00:44,850
to the surface
when they attack.

848
01:00:45,651 --> 01:00:47,153
If you are patient,

849
01:00:48,020 --> 01:00:50,089
we should see one.

850
01:00:50,189 --> 01:00:51,657
A worm always comes?

851
01:00:51,724 --> 01:00:54,527
Always. They're drawn
by rhythmic noises.

852
01:00:54,593 --> 01:00:56,696
Why don't we just shield
the crawlers?

853
01:00:56,762 --> 01:00:59,265
A shield's a death sentence
in the desert.

854
01:00:59,365 --> 01:01:00,599
It attracts the worms

855
01:01:00,700 --> 01:01:03,369
and drives them
into a killing frenzy.

856
01:01:06,105 --> 01:01:07,173
Is that a worm?

857
01:01:19,385 --> 01:01:21,187
[Dr. Kynes] Big one.

858
01:01:21,253 --> 01:01:23,589
You have good eyes.

859
01:01:23,689 --> 01:01:25,925
Calling crawler
Delta Ajax niner.

860
01:01:26,025 --> 01:01:28,527
Wormsign warning. Acknowledge.

861
01:01:28,594 --> 01:01:31,297
[Crawler over radio]
Who calls Delta Ajax niner?

862
01:01:31,397 --> 01:01:32,431
Over.

863
01:01:32,531 --> 01:01:33,933
They seem pretty calm
about it.

864
01:01:34,033 --> 01:01:36,535
[Dr. Kynes] Unlisted flight.
Imperium business.

865
01:01:36,602 --> 01:01:38,771
Wormsign north
and east of you.

866
01:01:38,871 --> 01:01:40,873
3.7 kilometers.

867
01:01:40,940 --> 01:01:42,475
[Spotter over radio]
Delta Ajax niner,

868
01:01:42,575 --> 01:01:44,376
this is Spotter One.
Wormsign confirmed.

869
01:01:45,745 --> 01:01:48,047
Stand by for contact fix.

870
01:01:51,584 --> 01:01:54,153
Worm is on intercept course
to your position.

871
01:01:54,253 --> 01:01:55,821
Contact in five minutes.

872
01:01:55,921 --> 01:01:57,723
So, what happens now?

873
01:01:57,790 --> 01:02:00,326
They'll call a carryall
to lift the crawler.

874
01:02:00,426 --> 01:02:02,561
They'll harvest right up
to the last minute.

875
01:02:02,628 --> 01:02:04,263
[Crawler]  Calling
carryall Alpha Zero.

876
01:02:04,330 --> 01:02:06,165
Ready for docking sequence.

877
01:02:06,265 --> 01:02:08,734
Contact five minutes. Over.

878
01:02:13,105 --> 01:02:15,241
[Spotter]  Anybody got a visual
on the carryall?

879
01:02:19,445 --> 01:02:20,946
[Dr. Kynes] There it is.

880
01:02:21,013 --> 01:02:22,348
[Carryall over radio]
This is carryall Alpha Zero

881
01:02:22,448 --> 01:02:24,784
to Delta Ajax niner.

882
01:02:24,850 --> 01:02:26,919
Approaching from your east.

883
01:02:26,986 --> 01:02:29,855
Correcting altitude and
preparing docking equipment.

884
01:02:29,955 --> 01:02:33,459
[Crawler]  Copy, Alpha Zero.
Initiating docking sequence.

885
01:02:35,494 --> 01:02:36,996
[Carryall]  T-5.

886
01:02:37,096 --> 01:02:38,531
[man]  Copy that.

887
01:02:38,631 --> 01:02:40,366
[Crawler]  Prepare
to be airborne in 30 seconds.

888
01:02:40,466 --> 01:02:42,768
[Carryall]  Docking sequence
initiated. Brace yourselves.

889
01:02:44,470 --> 01:02:46,038
[explosion]

890
01:02:46,138 --> 01:02:48,174
[man]  Alpha Zero, we're short
one point of contact.

891
01:02:48,274 --> 01:02:49,708
[Crawler]  What is going on?

892
01:02:49,809 --> 01:02:51,811
[Carryall]  It's one of
the anchors. It's dead.

893
01:02:52,812 --> 01:02:54,180
[Dr. Kynes] Shit.

894
01:02:54,280 --> 01:02:56,315
[Carryall]  Carryall
unable to receive.

895
01:02:56,382 --> 01:02:58,284
Unable to lift
without that anchor.

896
01:02:58,350 --> 01:03:00,052
[Crawler]  All call! All call!

897
01:03:00,152 --> 01:03:03,122
Any carryall in the sector,
please respond!

898
01:03:03,189 --> 01:03:05,157
Spotter One,
give us an update. Over.

899
01:03:05,224 --> 01:03:06,692
[Carryall]  Hydraulics are dead.

900
01:03:06,792 --> 01:03:08,360
We won't make it.
You have to evacuate.

901
01:03:08,460 --> 01:03:09,528
[announcer over radio]
Contact in four minutes.

902
01:03:09,628 --> 01:03:10,563
[Crawler]  Try it again!

903
01:03:10,663 --> 01:03:11,363
How many men on that crawler?

904
01:03:11,463 --> 01:03:12,531
Crew of 21.

905
01:03:12,631 --> 01:03:13,632
[Leto] Our ships
can take six each.

906
01:03:13,699 --> 01:03:14,867
That's still three short.

907
01:03:15,568 --> 01:03:16,635
We'll find a way.

908
01:03:28,914 --> 01:03:31,183
[over radio]
This is Duke Leto Atreides.

909
01:03:31,250 --> 01:03:34,887
We're coming down to extract
the crew of Delta Ajax niner.

910
01:03:34,987 --> 01:03:36,989
We'll set down on the west.

911
01:03:47,266 --> 01:03:49,268
Shield generators
weigh 100 kilos each.

912
01:03:50,035 --> 01:03:51,403
Yes, Gurney,

913
01:03:51,503 --> 01:03:52,771
have our escorts throw out
the shield generators.

914
01:03:52,872 --> 01:03:54,406
[Gurney] Yes, sire.

915
01:03:54,506 --> 01:03:56,075
[Leto] And, Paul, I want you
at the back of the thopter.

916
01:03:56,175 --> 01:03:57,243
Guide them in.

917
01:03:57,343 --> 01:03:58,544
Delta Ajax niner,

918
01:03:58,611 --> 01:04:01,113
put seven men each
in my ships now.

919
01:04:01,213 --> 01:04:03,449
[suspenseful music playing]

920
01:04:27,740 --> 01:04:29,909
[ethereal music playing]

921
01:04:46,091 --> 01:04:47,993
[machinery clanking]

922
01:04:59,438 --> 01:05:01,473
[announcer over radio]
Contact in two minutes.

923
01:05:01,573 --> 01:05:03,475
[indistinct radio chatter]

924
01:05:03,575 --> 01:05:06,412
[Spotter]  Getting close, guys.
We better abandon ship now.

925
01:05:06,478 --> 01:05:08,681
[indistinct radio chatter]

926
01:05:08,781 --> 01:05:10,082
Where are they?

927
01:05:10,149 --> 01:05:12,184
[Crawler]  Sir,
there's protocol for a reason.

928
01:05:12,284 --> 01:05:14,987
If we take one step out there,
we're as good as dead.

929
01:05:15,087 --> 01:05:16,689
Besides, we've got
a full load of spice.

930
01:05:16,789 --> 01:05:18,824
-We can't just leave it.
-Damn the spice!

931
01:05:18,924 --> 01:05:21,527
I want every man
off that crawler now!

932
01:05:25,164 --> 01:05:27,266
[tense music playing]

933
01:05:35,507 --> 01:05:36,608
Hey!

934
01:05:36,675 --> 01:05:37,776
Hey!

935
01:05:37,843 --> 01:05:40,379
Seven over here,
seven over there.

936
01:05:42,314 --> 01:05:44,717
Go! Go! Go!

937
01:05:44,817 --> 01:05:46,118
[tense music stops]

938
01:05:48,187 --> 01:05:50,289
[ethereal music playing]

939
01:05:57,696 --> 01:05:59,565
[eerie voices murmur]

940
01:05:59,665 --> 01:06:02,634
[eerie voices]
Kwisatz Haderach.

941
01:06:04,470 --> 01:06:06,805
[eerie voices murmuring
indistinctly]

942
01:06:15,814 --> 01:06:19,251
Kwisatz Haderach  awakes.

943
01:06:19,351 --> 01:06:21,420
[tense music playing]

944
01:06:28,727 --> 01:06:30,095
[Gurney] Hurry! Get on!

945
01:06:30,195 --> 01:06:31,730
[men shout hurriedly]

946
01:06:38,771 --> 01:06:39,872
[Dr. Kynes] It's here!

947
01:06:42,841 --> 01:06:43,876
[Leto] Paul!

948
01:06:46,345 --> 01:06:47,579
Paul!

949
01:06:51,417 --> 01:06:54,853
[quietly] I recognize
your footsteps, old man.

950
01:06:55,521 --> 01:06:57,089
Get up!

951
01:06:57,189 --> 01:06:59,725
Let's go!

952
01:06:59,792 --> 01:07:02,428
What's the matter with you?
Come on! Let's go!

953
01:07:02,528 --> 01:07:03,762
Run!

954
01:07:04,696 --> 01:07:06,765
[tense music continues]

955
01:07:12,571 --> 01:07:13,739
[grunting]

956
01:07:29,455 --> 01:07:30,489
[Gurney] Hey!

957
01:07:49,007 --> 01:07:51,443
Bless the Maker and His Water.

958
01:07:51,510 --> 01:07:53,745
Bless the coming
and going of Him.

959
01:07:53,812 --> 01:07:56,748
May His passage
cleanse the world

960
01:07:56,815 --> 01:07:59,318
and keep the world
for His people.

961
01:08:09,361 --> 01:08:11,296
[sandworm roars]

962
01:08:23,308 --> 01:08:24,543
Hey!

963
01:08:24,643 --> 01:08:26,678
-You cannot take such risks.
-[Paul] Yes, sir.

964
01:08:26,778 --> 01:08:28,046
You have responsibilities.

965
01:08:28,147 --> 01:08:29,281
I... I'm sorry, sir.
It won't happen again.

966
01:08:29,348 --> 01:08:30,349
Go.

967
01:08:31,183 --> 01:08:32,484
Dr. Kynes.

968
01:08:34,319 --> 01:08:36,155
You saw it.

969
01:08:36,221 --> 01:08:38,223
With your own eyes.
It's plain to see.

970
01:08:38,323 --> 01:08:40,559
Everything they've left us
is in shambles.

971
01:08:40,659 --> 01:08:42,561
We've been set up to fail.

972
01:08:42,661 --> 01:08:45,364
That carryall was just old.

973
01:08:45,464 --> 01:08:47,499
The desert
isn't kind to equipment.

974
01:08:49,368 --> 01:08:50,903
You know what will happen

975
01:08:51,003 --> 01:08:53,505
if I don't get spice
production back on track.

976
01:08:53,572 --> 01:08:55,374
[scoffs]

977
01:08:55,474 --> 01:08:59,311
I'm not here
to take your part.

978
01:08:59,378 --> 01:09:03,415
Arrakis has seen men like you
come and go.

979
01:09:06,051 --> 01:09:09,688
Take good care of your family.

980
01:09:13,025 --> 01:09:16,161
The desert's not kind
to humans either.

981
01:09:32,544 --> 01:09:35,614
Spice is a psychoactive
chemical.

982
01:09:36,782 --> 01:09:38,750
You seem to be sensitive.

983
01:09:43,121 --> 01:09:44,189
You'll be fine.

984
01:09:45,891 --> 01:09:47,926
Thank you, Dr. Yueh.

985
01:09:57,302 --> 01:09:59,805
That wasn't
an allergic reaction.

986
01:10:01,740 --> 01:10:03,408
I had a vision.

987
01:10:05,911 --> 01:10:07,646
My eyes were wide open.

988
01:10:09,615 --> 01:10:10,649
What did you see?

989
01:10:17,422 --> 01:10:19,491
[eerie ethereal music playing]

990
01:10:48,120 --> 01:10:51,857
[eerie voices]
Kwisatz Haderach.

991
01:10:51,957 --> 01:10:54,993
You can see.

992
01:11:36,401 --> 01:11:38,070
[Paul]  It's confusing.

993
01:11:38,170 --> 01:11:39,705
I thought I saw my death,

994
01:11:39,805 --> 01:11:41,973
only it wasn't.

995
01:11:42,040 --> 01:11:45,911
I know a knife is important,
somehow.

996
01:11:47,846 --> 01:11:50,215
Someone will hand me a blade,

997
01:11:50,315 --> 01:11:54,019
but I don't know who,
or when, or where.

998
01:11:56,088 --> 01:11:59,091
Some things, though,
are crystal clear.

999
01:11:59,191 --> 01:12:00,525
I can feel it.

1000
01:12:05,230 --> 01:12:06,765
I know you're pregnant.

1001
01:12:12,871 --> 01:12:14,673
You can't know that.

1002
01:12:16,208 --> 01:12:17,409
I barely know that.

1003
01:12:17,509 --> 01:12:19,511
It's only been a few weeks.

1004
01:12:29,688 --> 01:12:32,257
[priest throat-singing
in Sardaukar]

1005
01:13:02,087 --> 01:13:04,256
[Bashar speaking Sardaukar]

1006
01:13:10,629 --> 01:13:11,897
[Piter in English]
Atreides legions

1007
01:13:11,963 --> 01:13:14,299
are the finest
in the Imperium.

1008
01:13:14,399 --> 01:13:16,768
Trained by Gurney Halleck
and Duncan Idaho.

1009
01:13:18,003 --> 01:13:19,805
[speaking Sardaukar]

1010
01:13:25,243 --> 01:13:26,678
[in English] Just so.

1011
01:13:27,579 --> 01:13:29,247
Three battalions.

1012
01:13:29,314 --> 01:13:30,348
As agreed.

1013
01:13:30,449 --> 01:13:32,017
[continues throat-singing]

1014
01:13:33,585 --> 01:13:35,187
[all grunt]

1015
01:13:35,287 --> 01:13:37,355
[speaking Sardaukar]

1016
01:13:45,864 --> 01:13:48,099
[whimpering]

1017
01:13:53,505 --> 01:13:55,540
[crying softly]

1018
01:14:10,822 --> 01:14:13,058
There is something
you need to know about Paul.

1019
01:14:13,158 --> 01:14:15,060
[Leto] No.

1020
01:14:15,160 --> 01:14:17,562
Don't think I want to know.

1021
01:14:17,662 --> 01:14:19,664
Ever since you brought him
before your Reverend Mother,

1022
01:14:19,731 --> 01:14:21,566
he hasn't been the same.

1023
01:14:23,235 --> 01:14:24,536
He's distracted.

1024
01:14:26,471 --> 01:14:29,574
Jessica, you gave me a son.

1025
01:14:29,674 --> 01:14:31,042
And from the moment
he was born,

1026
01:14:31,142 --> 01:14:33,011
I never questioned you.

1027
01:14:33,078 --> 01:14:35,547
I trusted you completely.

1028
01:14:35,647 --> 01:14:37,816
Even when
you walked in shadows.

1029
01:14:38,984 --> 01:14:40,919
Now I'm asking you
this one thing.

1030
01:14:43,555 --> 01:14:45,724
If anything happens...

1031
01:14:46,825 --> 01:14:48,193
will you protect our son?

1032
01:14:49,928 --> 01:14:51,429
With my life.

1033
01:14:51,530 --> 01:14:53,932
I'm not asking his mother.
I'm asking the Bene Gesserit.

1034
01:14:58,169 --> 01:15:00,205
Will you protect Paul?

1035
01:15:05,777 --> 01:15:07,779
Why are you
having these thoughts?

1036
01:15:14,252 --> 01:15:16,788
Leto, this is not you.

1037
01:15:22,394 --> 01:15:24,796
I thought we'd have more time.

1038
01:15:43,748 --> 01:15:46,384
[Dr. Yueh] Have a good night,
Master Paul.

1039
01:15:46,451 --> 01:15:48,386
[Paul] Good night, Dr. Yueh.

1040
01:15:57,662 --> 01:15:59,097
[Lady Jessica]
You need to sleep.

1041
01:16:00,932 --> 01:16:02,300
No.

1042
01:16:02,400 --> 01:16:03,668
Not like that.

1043
01:16:06,471 --> 01:16:08,506
[Leto sighs deeply]

1044
01:16:18,950 --> 01:16:21,186
I should have married you.

1045
01:16:25,957 --> 01:16:28,093
[footsteps]

1046
01:16:29,094 --> 01:16:30,495
[weapon firing]

1047
01:16:32,330 --> 01:16:34,199
[guards groaning]

1048
01:16:39,337 --> 01:16:40,805
[wheezing]

1049
01:16:48,146 --> 01:16:50,281
[shield powering down]

1050
01:16:56,021 --> 01:16:58,123
[low tense music playing]

1051
01:17:32,190 --> 01:17:33,391
[soft grunt]

1052
01:17:39,431 --> 01:17:41,199
[softly] Hawat. Security.

1053
01:17:43,535 --> 01:17:44,936
[normal tone] Security.

1054
01:17:53,278 --> 01:17:54,946
[device beeps]

1055
01:17:59,784 --> 01:18:01,619
[choking]

1056
01:18:07,625 --> 01:18:08,760
[stifled grunt]

1057
01:18:13,131 --> 01:18:14,132
[dart fires]

1058
01:18:14,232 --> 01:18:16,267
[shield crackling]

1059
01:18:23,942 --> 01:18:25,910
[groaning]

1060
01:18:34,552 --> 01:18:36,621
[tense music playing]

1061
01:18:37,956 --> 01:18:39,090
[whimpers]

1062
01:18:47,832 --> 01:18:49,501
[Lieutenant] Sir. Sir.

1063
01:18:50,401 --> 01:18:52,170
The shield's come down.

1064
01:18:52,270 --> 01:18:54,506
-[alarm blaring]
-[soldiers clamoring]

1065
01:19:01,079 --> 01:19:03,014
[Gurney] God in heaven.

1066
01:19:03,114 --> 01:19:06,084
Get everything with guns
off the ground! Go!

1067
01:19:06,151 --> 01:19:08,286
[soldiers shouting]

1068
01:19:08,353 --> 01:19:10,655
[dramatic music playing]

1069
01:19:12,290 --> 01:19:13,424
[missile whistles]

1070
01:19:50,061 --> 01:19:51,863
Go! Go! Go!

1071
01:19:52,664 --> 01:19:54,465
[soldiers screaming]

1072
01:20:14,519 --> 01:20:15,720
[missile whistles]

1073
01:20:48,586 --> 01:20:50,221
[grunting]

1074
01:20:52,257 --> 01:20:53,691
[groans]

1075
01:20:53,758 --> 01:20:55,760
With me! With me!

1076
01:20:56,561 --> 01:20:58,463
[soldiers yelling]

1077
01:20:59,697 --> 01:21:01,766
[dramatic music continues]

1078
01:21:21,486 --> 01:21:23,221
[marching footsteps]

1079
01:21:24,756 --> 01:21:25,823
[Lieutenant] Atreides!

1080
01:21:25,924 --> 01:21:27,091
[guards] Atreides!

1081
01:21:31,095 --> 01:21:33,064
[all grunting in unison]

1082
01:21:34,666 --> 01:21:36,768
[synchronized grunting]

1083
01:21:40,305 --> 01:21:41,639
[all grunting]

1084
01:21:55,954 --> 01:21:58,323
-[Atreides guard 1] Sardaukar!
-[Atreides guard 2] Sardaukar!

1085
01:22:01,960 --> 01:22:03,494
[groaning]

1086
01:22:21,813 --> 01:22:23,481
I'm sorry, my lord.

1087
01:22:26,317 --> 01:22:29,287
But I've made a bargain
with the Baron.

1088
01:22:29,354 --> 01:22:31,723
[Leto breathing raggedly]

1089
01:22:31,823 --> 01:22:32,824
Why?

1090
01:22:33,691 --> 01:22:35,727
I had no choice.

1091
01:22:35,827 --> 01:22:39,664
The Harkonnens
have my wife, Wanna.

1092
01:22:39,731 --> 01:22:42,300
They take her apart
like a doll.

1093
01:22:43,301 --> 01:22:45,403
I will buy her freedom.

1094
01:22:45,503 --> 01:22:47,071
And you are the price.

1095
01:22:50,408 --> 01:22:53,478
For Paul.
I will do what I can.

1096
01:22:54,178 --> 01:22:55,880
And you

1097
01:22:55,980 --> 01:22:57,849
will kill a man for me.

1098
01:23:02,220 --> 01:23:05,757
I'm going to replace
your peg tooth.

1099
01:23:05,857 --> 01:23:10,762
If you bite down hard,
this tooth will crush.

1100
01:23:10,862 --> 01:23:15,099
Breathe out, and you will
fill the air with poison.

1101
01:23:15,199 --> 01:23:17,902
It will be your last breath.

1102
01:23:18,002 --> 01:23:20,338
But if you choose
your moment well,

1103
01:23:21,606 --> 01:23:23,908
it will also be the Baron's.

1104
01:23:42,293 --> 01:23:44,295
[tense music playing]

1105
01:24:02,146 --> 01:24:03,548
[yelling]

1106
01:24:24,102 --> 01:24:25,603
[soldiers speak indistinctly]

1107
01:24:34,745 --> 01:24:35,847
[soldier groans]

1108
01:24:38,783 --> 01:24:39,784
[grunts]

1109
01:24:57,635 --> 01:24:58,703
Paul.

1110
01:25:09,280 --> 01:25:11,015
[door closes]

1111
01:25:12,517 --> 01:25:14,719
[trooper 1 speaking Harkonnen]

1112
01:25:20,158 --> 01:25:21,392
[trooper 2 speaking]

1113
01:25:23,528 --> 01:25:25,029
[trooper 1 speaking]

1114
01:25:37,708 --> 01:25:38,809
[in sign language]

1115
01:26:14,445 --> 01:26:16,447
[all grunting]

1116
01:26:21,552 --> 01:26:23,287
[Duncan] To hell, dogs!

1117
01:26:25,122 --> 01:26:26,123
[grunts]

1118
01:26:44,075 --> 01:26:45,443
[alarm beeping]

1119
01:27:58,883 --> 01:28:01,686
[trooper 1 in English]
I've never had a highborn.

1120
01:28:04,055 --> 01:28:05,389
You?

1121
01:28:05,489 --> 01:28:07,558
Bene Gesserit
ain't all highborn.

1122
01:28:07,658 --> 01:28:11,462
[trooper 1]
She's highborn enough for me.

1123
01:28:11,529 --> 01:28:13,798
Let's feed the kid
to the worms.

1124
01:28:13,864 --> 01:28:15,866
And give her a long goodbye.

1125
01:28:15,966 --> 01:28:17,735
Don't you dare
touch my mother.

1126
01:28:19,203 --> 01:28:20,237
Don't talk.

1127
01:28:26,510 --> 01:28:27,845
[in sign language]

1128
01:28:29,180 --> 01:28:30,715
[Paul sighs]

1129
01:28:31,582 --> 01:28:33,084
[sternly] Remove her gag.

1130
01:28:41,192 --> 01:28:42,093
[retches]

1131
01:28:42,193 --> 01:28:43,994
[trooper 1] Shut up.

1132
01:28:45,096 --> 01:28:46,364
[in sign language]

1133
01:28:47,365 --> 01:28:49,333
[panting]

1134
01:28:54,338 --> 01:28:55,840
[trooper 1 speaking Harkonnen]

1135
01:28:58,776 --> 01:29:00,378
[Paul breathing deeply]

1136
01:29:12,923 --> 01:29:14,191
[in distorted voice]
Remove her gag.

1137
01:29:20,264 --> 01:29:21,465
[in distorted voice] Kill him.

1138
01:29:30,441 --> 01:29:31,609
[in distorted voice]
Set us free.

1139
01:29:36,914 --> 01:29:39,383
[speaking Harkonnen]

1140
01:29:41,152 --> 01:29:42,386
[trooper 1 groans]

1141
01:29:43,421 --> 01:29:44,989
[Lady Jessica grunting]

1142
01:29:45,089 --> 01:29:46,424
[in distorted voice] Stop!

1143
01:29:46,490 --> 01:29:48,058
Cut the rope.

1144
01:29:50,761 --> 01:29:52,229
Give me the knife.

1145
01:29:52,830 --> 01:29:54,131
[stabs]

1146
01:29:56,400 --> 01:29:57,468
[grunts]

1147
01:30:00,938 --> 01:30:04,008
[in normal voice]
Your pitch was too forced.

1148
01:30:11,916 --> 01:30:13,484
[Paul] It's a fremkit.

1149
01:30:17,455 --> 01:30:20,024
[man speaks Harkonnen
over radio]

1150
01:30:24,161 --> 01:30:26,363
[engine shuts off]

1151
01:30:26,464 --> 01:30:27,665
They've crippled the ship.

1152
01:30:43,347 --> 01:30:44,515
[distant explosions]

1153
01:30:53,324 --> 01:30:54,625
[gasping]

1154
01:30:59,630 --> 01:31:00,831
[sighs]

1155
01:31:16,413 --> 01:31:18,148
[explosions continue]

1156
01:31:36,033 --> 01:31:37,835
[wheezing softly]

1157
01:31:40,704 --> 01:31:41,872
[man] Mmm.

1158
01:31:47,945 --> 01:31:49,380
[Vladimir grunts softly]

1159
01:31:51,916 --> 01:31:54,018
[cutlery clinking]

1160
01:31:54,084 --> 01:31:55,252
[Vladimir grunts]

1161
01:32:00,190 --> 01:32:01,592
Ah.

1162
01:32:01,692 --> 01:32:02,960
[munching]

1163
01:32:03,060 --> 01:32:06,130
You have a wonderful kitchen,
cousin.

1164
01:32:07,197 --> 01:32:09,033
[wind howling]

1165
01:32:13,771 --> 01:32:15,039
[Paul grunts]

1166
01:32:24,315 --> 01:32:27,151
This is Dr. Yueh's
handwriting.

1167
01:32:27,251 --> 01:32:29,820
"If anyone makes it out
of Arrakeen alive,

1168
01:32:29,920 --> 01:32:32,056
there's an Atreides beacon
in the fremkit.

1169
01:32:32,122 --> 01:32:34,892
God willing,
they'll be able to find you."

1170
01:32:38,762 --> 01:32:40,431
[wheezing weakly]

1171
01:32:42,232 --> 01:32:43,267
My lord Baron.

1172
01:32:44,668 --> 01:32:45,836
Dr. Yueh.

1173
01:32:45,936 --> 01:32:47,605
[Vladimir] The traitor.

1174
01:32:48,806 --> 01:32:49,940
What do you want?

1175
01:32:51,108 --> 01:32:53,344
I jammed their comms

1176
01:32:53,444 --> 01:32:55,446
and lowered their shields.

1177
01:32:55,512 --> 01:32:56,780
[Vladimir] Hmm.

1178
01:32:56,847 --> 01:32:59,116
[Dr. Yueh] I delivered
the Duke and his family.

1179
01:32:59,183 --> 01:33:01,685
[Vladimir] The bargain
to the letter.

1180
01:33:01,785 --> 01:33:04,288
And what was I to do for you?

1181
01:33:04,355 --> 01:33:06,523
Deliver my wife
from her agony.

1182
01:33:08,459 --> 01:33:09,526
[Vladimir] Yes.

1183
01:33:11,962 --> 01:33:14,031
[slow sinister music playing]

1184
01:33:38,455 --> 01:33:40,324
[chewing loudly]

1185
01:33:42,993 --> 01:33:45,629
I said I'd set her free.

1186
01:33:45,696 --> 01:33:47,531
That you could join her.

1187
01:33:50,501 --> 01:33:51,568
[Dr. Yueh grunts]

1188
01:33:51,669 --> 01:33:53,570
So, join her.

1189
01:33:53,671 --> 01:33:55,539
-[knife slices]
-[body thuds]

1190
01:34:02,479 --> 01:34:04,715
What do you think is next?

1191
01:34:08,385 --> 01:34:10,688
[Paul] It's a thumper.

1192
01:34:10,754 --> 01:34:12,356
No stillsuits.

1193
01:34:12,423 --> 01:34:14,358
The one thing
we actually need.

1194
01:34:19,430 --> 01:34:23,033
For hundreds of years,
we've traded blood for blood.

1195
01:34:24,234 --> 01:34:25,903
But no more.

1196
01:34:27,371 --> 01:34:31,608
Your son is dead.
Your concubine is dead.

1197
01:34:31,709 --> 01:34:34,578
Tonight
the House of Atreides falls.

1198
01:34:37,381 --> 01:34:40,451
And your bloodline
ends forever.

1199
01:34:42,286 --> 01:34:44,254
[Leto mumbling]

1200
01:34:53,630 --> 01:34:54,698
What did you say?

1201
01:35:04,742 --> 01:35:06,210
[softly] Here I am...

1202
01:35:07,478 --> 01:35:09,279
here I remain.

1203
01:35:10,948 --> 01:35:12,382
[tooth crunches]

1204
01:35:12,449 --> 01:35:13,984
[exhales forcefully]

1205
01:35:14,084 --> 01:35:16,086
-[gasping]
-[dramatic music playing]

1206
01:35:18,889 --> 01:35:19,990
[Piter coughs]

1207
01:35:38,909 --> 01:35:40,077
[cries softly]

1208
01:36:00,164 --> 01:36:02,266
[soft music playing]

1209
01:36:21,318 --> 01:36:23,687
[dramatic lamentation music
playing]

1210
01:36:36,867 --> 01:36:38,502
[engine roaring in distance]

1211
01:36:52,516 --> 01:36:53,717
[Duncan] Kynes!

1212
01:36:54,985 --> 01:36:56,753
It's not safe for you here.

1213
01:36:56,854 --> 01:36:58,088
[Duncan] Will you tell
the Great Houses

1214
01:36:58,188 --> 01:36:59,656
of the Landsraad
how we were betrayed?

1215
01:36:59,723 --> 01:37:02,326
How the best of them
were murdered?

1216
01:37:02,392 --> 01:37:05,062
I am commanded to say nothing.

1217
01:37:06,029 --> 01:37:07,731
To see nothing.

1218
01:37:09,566 --> 01:37:11,935
The Emperor
sent us here to die.

1219
01:37:12,035 --> 01:37:14,171
[lamentation music continues]

1220
01:37:36,293 --> 01:37:38,061
[man choking]

1221
01:37:41,064 --> 01:37:43,100
[strained breathing]

1222
01:37:57,414 --> 01:37:58,916
[coughing]

1223
01:38:00,150 --> 01:38:02,552
[Paul] There's spice
in the tent.

1224
01:38:10,894 --> 01:38:12,562
[coughing]

1225
01:38:13,430 --> 01:38:14,564
[clears throat]

1226
01:38:22,439 --> 01:38:24,675
[slow dramatic music playing]

1227
01:38:35,118 --> 01:38:37,454
[voices whispering
indistinctly]

1228
01:38:49,633 --> 01:38:51,868
[soldiers clamoring]

1229
01:39:13,657 --> 01:39:15,659
[panting]

1230
01:39:18,295 --> 01:39:20,497
[slow ominous music playing]

1231
01:39:28,171 --> 01:39:31,141
That's the future.
It's coming.

1232
01:39:34,878 --> 01:39:36,980
[ominous music continues]

1233
01:39:45,689 --> 01:39:47,891
Holy war
spreading across the universe

1234
01:39:47,991 --> 01:39:49,259
like unquenchable fire.

1235
01:39:51,361 --> 01:39:53,430
[voices continue whispering]

1236
01:39:59,536 --> 01:40:02,105
[thunder rumbling]

1237
01:40:02,205 --> 01:40:05,108
Paul, you're scared.
I can see it.

1238
01:40:05,208 --> 01:40:08,278
Tell me, please,
what do you fear?

1239
01:40:08,378 --> 01:40:10,514
[voices continue whispering]

1240
01:40:17,254 --> 01:40:19,756
Somebody help me, please.

1241
01:40:20,457 --> 01:40:21,625
Paul.

1242
01:40:23,927 --> 01:40:25,629
It's coming.

1243
01:40:25,729 --> 01:40:27,130
I see a holy war spreading

1244
01:40:27,230 --> 01:40:29,132
across the universe
like unquenchable fire.

1245
01:40:29,232 --> 01:40:32,235
A warrior religion
that waves the Atreides banner

1246
01:40:32,302 --> 01:40:33,470
in my father's name.

1247
01:40:33,570 --> 01:40:34,471
[Lady Jessica] Paul.

1248
01:40:34,571 --> 01:40:36,239
Fanatical legions worshipping

1249
01:40:36,306 --> 01:40:38,475
at the shrine
of my father's skull.

1250
01:40:39,309 --> 01:40:41,778
A war in my name!

1251
01:40:41,878 --> 01:40:43,713
Everyone's shouting my name!

1252
01:40:43,780 --> 01:40:44,781
Paul.

1253
01:40:48,452 --> 01:40:50,554
Paul Atreides.

1254
01:40:50,620 --> 01:40:53,590
You are your father's son.
You are my son.

1255
01:40:53,657 --> 01:40:57,160
You are
the Duke Paul Atreides.

1256
01:40:57,260 --> 01:41:00,063
You know who you are.
You know who you are.

1257
01:41:00,130 --> 01:41:01,298
[in distorted voice]
Get off me!

1258
01:41:03,233 --> 01:41:04,901
[normal voice]
You did this to me!

1259
01:41:04,968 --> 01:41:07,671
You Bene Gesserit
made me a freak!

1260
01:41:15,011 --> 01:41:17,114
[breathing heavily]

1261
01:41:25,655 --> 01:41:27,691
[Paul crying]

1262
01:41:32,796 --> 01:41:35,098
My father is dead.

1263
01:41:35,165 --> 01:41:37,200
[Paul sobbing]

1264
01:41:42,472 --> 01:41:44,774
[mournful music playing]

1265
01:42:05,662 --> 01:42:07,697
[device beeping]

1266
01:42:11,568 --> 01:42:13,069
[Paul softly] Someone's near.

1267
01:42:14,004 --> 01:42:15,505
You need to drink.

1268
01:42:17,073 --> 01:42:19,376
It's recycled water
from the tent.

1269
01:42:27,184 --> 01:42:28,985
Sweat and tears.

1270
01:42:32,656 --> 01:42:34,357
All right,
let's get out of here.

1271
01:42:38,028 --> 01:42:40,063
[device whirring]

1272
01:42:41,364 --> 01:42:43,400
[shield buzzing]

1273
01:42:53,176 --> 01:42:54,411
[shield buzzing]

1274
01:42:59,716 --> 01:43:01,384
[squeaks]

1275
01:43:04,387 --> 01:43:05,922
[whimpers]

1276
01:43:10,060 --> 01:43:12,128
[muffled whirring]

1277
01:43:16,633 --> 01:43:18,268
[grunting and panting]

1278
01:43:27,644 --> 01:43:28,812
[squeaks]

1279
01:43:32,215 --> 01:43:33,550
[Paul grunts]

1280
01:43:34,484 --> 01:43:36,553
[Lady Jessica panting]

1281
01:43:36,620 --> 01:43:38,455
[engine roaring]

1282
01:43:47,597 --> 01:43:49,332
That's Duncan.

1283
01:43:56,439 --> 01:43:57,674
Duncan.

1284
01:43:57,774 --> 01:43:59,242
[panting]

1285
01:43:59,309 --> 01:44:00,510
My lady.

1286
01:44:00,610 --> 01:44:02,012
Paul.

1287
01:44:02,112 --> 01:44:04,481
I'm so sorry. Your father...

1288
01:44:04,581 --> 01:44:05,782
We know.

1289
01:44:07,684 --> 01:44:09,019
My lord Duke.

1290
01:44:22,799 --> 01:44:23,800
Here.

1291
01:44:25,869 --> 01:44:27,370
Drink this.

1292
01:44:34,644 --> 01:44:37,013
[Duncan] Harkonnens hit
every population center

1293
01:44:37,113 --> 01:44:38,548
on the planet at once.

1294
01:44:38,648 --> 01:44:40,784
There must have been
10 legions, hundreds of ships.

1295
01:44:40,850 --> 01:44:42,886
There were Sardaukar
with them.

1296
01:44:42,986 --> 01:44:45,522
-At least two battalions.
-What? Are you sure?

1297
01:44:45,622 --> 01:44:48,291
You cross swords
with a Sardaukar,

1298
01:44:48,358 --> 01:44:49,726
you know it.

1299
01:44:49,826 --> 01:44:54,564
[Lady Jessica sighs] So,
the Emperor's taken a side.

1300
01:44:54,664 --> 01:44:57,801
What says
the Judge of the Change?

1301
01:44:57,867 --> 01:44:59,903
The Emperor forbids me
from saying anything at all.

1302
01:45:00,003 --> 01:45:01,971
And yet you risk your life
to help us.

1303
01:45:10,413 --> 01:45:11,715
[thunder rumbling]

1304
01:45:16,820 --> 01:45:18,588
[man shouting]

1305
01:45:20,423 --> 01:45:22,359
-[thunder continues rumbling]
-[clamoring]

1306
01:45:22,425 --> 01:45:24,160
[worker] Storm's coming.

1307
01:45:27,230 --> 01:45:28,932
[workers shouting
indistinctly]

1308
01:45:38,041 --> 01:45:40,276
[Dr. Kynes] The storm
will be here in a few hours.

1309
01:45:40,377 --> 01:45:41,511
We'll be safe here.

1310
01:45:43,046 --> 01:45:45,281
Do you know
what this place is?

1311
01:45:45,382 --> 01:45:47,784
It's an old
ecological testing station.

1312
01:45:51,187 --> 01:45:53,022
They were meant
to tame the planet.

1313
01:45:53,089 --> 01:45:55,525
Free the water
locked beneath the sands.

1314
01:45:58,528 --> 01:46:01,131
Arrakis could have been
a paradise.

1315
01:46:01,231 --> 01:46:02,365
The work had begun,

1316
01:46:02,432 --> 01:46:04,100
but then the spice
was discovered.

1317
01:46:04,200 --> 01:46:07,203
And suddenly no one
wanted the desert to go away.

1318
01:46:07,270 --> 01:46:08,471
Tanat,

1319
01:46:08,571 --> 01:46:10,140
will you find stillsuits
to fit our visitors?

1320
01:46:10,240 --> 01:46:11,474
TANAT: Yes, Liet.

1321
01:46:11,574 --> 01:46:12,976
[Dr. Kynes] Shamir,
a coffee service, please.

1322
01:46:13,076 --> 01:46:14,544
SHAMIR: Of course, Liet.

1323
01:46:15,612 --> 01:46:16,780
[door unlocks]

1324
01:46:16,880 --> 01:46:18,782
Who are you to the Fremen?

1325
01:46:44,340 --> 01:46:46,443
[indistinct chatter]

1326
01:46:56,119 --> 01:46:58,021
[wind howling]

1327
01:47:08,798 --> 01:47:10,533
[Paul] You know what
the Great Houses fear most,

1328
01:47:10,633 --> 01:47:12,202
Dr. Kynes?

1329
01:47:13,470 --> 01:47:15,705
Exactly what has happened
to us here.

1330
01:47:16,706 --> 01:47:17,874
The Sardaukar coming

1331
01:47:17,974 --> 01:47:19,676
and picking them off
one by one.

1332
01:47:22,645 --> 01:47:24,280
Only together
can they stand a chance

1333
01:47:24,347 --> 01:47:25,849
against the Imperium.

1334
01:47:27,884 --> 01:47:30,053
Would you bear witness?

1335
01:47:30,153 --> 01:47:33,289
Testify that the Emperor
has moved against us here?

1336
01:47:33,356 --> 01:47:36,292
If they believe me,

1337
01:47:36,359 --> 01:47:38,061
there would be general warfare

1338
01:47:38,161 --> 01:47:40,363
between the Great Houses
and the Emperor.

1339
01:47:40,463 --> 01:47:42,031
Chaos

1340
01:47:42,131 --> 01:47:43,566
across the Imperium.

1341
01:47:43,666 --> 01:47:45,068
Suppose I presented
the Emperor

1342
01:47:45,168 --> 01:47:47,637
with an alternative to chaos.

1343
01:47:47,704 --> 01:47:49,639
The Emperor has no sons.

1344
01:47:49,706 --> 01:47:51,708
And his daughters
have yet to marry.

1345
01:47:51,808 --> 01:47:54,577
You'd make a play
for the throne?

1346
01:47:54,677 --> 01:47:56,412
The Emperor
feared the Atreides.

1347
01:47:56,513 --> 01:47:58,181
He brought you here
to kill you.

1348
01:47:58,248 --> 01:48:00,750
What don't you understand?

1349
01:48:00,850 --> 01:48:04,020
You're a lost boy hiding
in a hole in the ground.

1350
01:48:08,224 --> 01:48:10,994
The Fremen speak
of the  Lisan al-Gaib.

1351
01:48:11,995 --> 01:48:13,830
Careful.

1352
01:48:13,897 --> 01:48:15,064
The Voice from the Outer World

1353
01:48:15,164 --> 01:48:17,333
who will lead them
to paradise.

1354
01:48:18,668 --> 01:48:19,869
Superstition.

1355
01:48:24,674 --> 01:48:26,409
I know you loved
a Fremen warrior

1356
01:48:26,509 --> 01:48:27,777
and lost him in battle.

1357
01:48:31,014 --> 01:48:34,717
I know you walk in two worlds
and are known by many names.

1358
01:48:39,956 --> 01:48:41,858
I've seen your dream.

1359
01:48:45,962 --> 01:48:47,196
As emperor, Dr. Kynes,

1360
01:48:47,263 --> 01:48:49,198
I could make
a paradise of Arrakis

1361
01:48:49,265 --> 01:48:50,800
with a wave of my hand.

1362
01:48:53,403 --> 01:48:54,904
[man speaking Chakobsa]

1363
01:49:00,443 --> 01:49:01,477
[man 2 shushing]

1364
01:49:38,781 --> 01:49:41,351
[soldier speaking Sardaukar]

1365
01:49:41,451 --> 01:49:44,320
-[explosions]
-[all grunting]

1366
01:49:44,420 --> 01:49:46,089
-[blades slicing]
-[groaning]

1367
01:49:55,131 --> 01:49:57,266
[muffled thudding]

1368
01:49:58,267 --> 01:50:00,336
[suspenseful music playing]

1369
01:50:46,582 --> 01:50:47,650
Sardaukar!

1370
01:50:50,753 --> 01:50:51,988
No! Duncan!

1371
01:50:52,055 --> 01:50:53,322
[Lady Jessica] Paul, no!

1372
01:50:53,389 --> 01:50:54,691
-[Paul] Duncan, no!
-[Lady Jessica] No!

1373
01:50:55,858 --> 01:50:57,160
-[Paul] No!
-[Lady Jessica] Paul, no!

1374
01:50:58,361 --> 01:50:59,662
[Paul] Duncan, no!

1375
01:50:59,729 --> 01:51:02,198
-He's locked the door.
-[Paul] Duncan! No!

1376
01:51:05,201 --> 01:51:07,403
[slow choral music playing]

1377
01:51:11,941 --> 01:51:13,876
[all grunting]

1378
01:51:15,945 --> 01:51:17,680
[tense music playing]

1379
01:51:33,863 --> 01:51:34,964
[Duncan groans]

1380
01:51:41,070 --> 01:51:42,538
[soldier speaks Sardaukar]

1381
01:51:42,605 --> 01:51:44,407
[shield crackling]

1382
01:51:51,581 --> 01:51:53,149
He's gone.

1383
01:51:53,249 --> 01:51:54,317
[Paul] Duncan!

1384
01:51:54,417 --> 01:51:55,985
We have to go.
We have no choice.

1385
01:51:56,085 --> 01:51:57,887
[tense music continues]

1386
01:52:02,291 --> 01:52:03,493
[laser firing]

1387
01:52:03,593 --> 01:52:05,995
[Lady Jessica] Paul, go! Paul!

1388
01:52:19,509 --> 01:52:20,943
[Duncan yelling]

1389
01:52:24,914 --> 01:52:26,582
[Dr. Kynes] Come on.
Come on, come on!

1390
01:52:38,961 --> 01:52:40,963
[shield buzzing]

1391
01:52:42,498 --> 01:52:43,599
[speaks Sardaukar]

1392
01:52:47,804 --> 01:52:49,772
[tense music continues]

1393
01:52:57,947 --> 01:52:59,615
[panting] Follow the light.

1394
01:52:59,682 --> 01:53:01,884
You'll find a thopter
ready to fly.

1395
01:53:01,984 --> 01:53:03,853
That storm out there
is your best shot.

1396
01:53:03,953 --> 01:53:06,522
Above 5,000 meters,
it's mostly dust.

1397
01:53:06,622 --> 01:53:10,726
Climb into it. Stay on top.
Head south. Find the Fremen.

1398
01:53:10,827 --> 01:53:12,061
Are you not coming with us?

1399
01:53:12,161 --> 01:53:13,362
It only seats two.

1400
01:53:13,462 --> 01:53:15,164
I'll go to the next station

1401
01:53:15,231 --> 01:53:16,966
and report this attack
to the Landsraad.

1402
01:53:17,033 --> 01:53:18,334
[Lady Jessica] How?

1403
01:53:19,068 --> 01:53:21,003
I'm Fremen.

1404
01:53:21,070 --> 01:53:23,306
The desert's my home.

1405
01:53:23,372 --> 01:53:24,473
Good luck.

1406
01:53:24,540 --> 01:53:25,741
[Paul] Good luck.

1407
01:53:32,415 --> 01:53:34,417
[dramatic tense music playing]

1408
01:54:23,466 --> 01:54:25,368
[switches clicking]

1409
01:54:25,434 --> 01:54:27,136
[engine sputtering]

1410
01:54:31,941 --> 01:54:33,242
[engine rumbles]

1411
01:54:34,911 --> 01:54:36,479
[engine starts]

1412
01:55:36,939 --> 01:55:38,107
[blade stabs]

1413
01:55:39,942 --> 01:55:41,510
-[blade retracts]
-[groans]

1414
01:55:41,610 --> 01:55:44,113
[dramatic lamentation music
playing]

1415
01:56:03,833 --> 01:56:05,468
[assassin speaking Sardaukar]

1416
01:56:06,836 --> 01:56:09,238
[in English]
I serve only one master.

1417
01:56:09,338 --> 01:56:12,675
His name is  Shai-Hulud.

1418
01:56:13,976 --> 01:56:16,345
[pounding rhythmically]

1419
01:56:16,412 --> 01:56:17,513
[speaks Sardaukar]

1420
01:56:18,914 --> 01:56:20,216
[assassin grunts]

1421
01:56:21,050 --> 01:56:23,219
[assassins grunting]

1422
01:56:26,822 --> 01:56:28,257
[grunts]

1423
01:56:32,361 --> 01:56:34,363
[panicked chatter]

1424
01:56:34,430 --> 01:56:36,999
-[sandworm roars]
-[assassins screaming]

1425
01:56:50,212 --> 01:56:51,447
[switches click]

1426
01:56:54,850 --> 01:56:57,620
[ominous music playing]

1427
01:56:57,720 --> 01:56:59,288
There are jet flares
behind us.

1428
01:57:09,732 --> 01:57:11,300
[Lady Jessica grunting]

1429
01:57:25,214 --> 01:57:27,116
[alarm wailing]

1430
01:57:31,420 --> 01:57:33,055
[engine accelerating]

1431
01:57:33,122 --> 01:57:35,057
Paul. We're not high enough!

1432
01:57:41,964 --> 01:57:43,432
[missile whistling]

1433
01:57:45,334 --> 01:57:46,802
-[metal rattling]
-[explosion]

1434
01:57:49,972 --> 01:57:51,941
-[metallic clanking]
-[Paul gasps]

1435
01:57:58,514 --> 01:58:00,749
-[clanking continues]
-[metal squeaks]

1436
01:58:00,816 --> 01:58:02,485
[engine rumbling]

1437
01:58:04,120 --> 01:58:05,754
[metal rattling]

1438
01:58:07,790 --> 01:58:09,125
I must not fear.

1439
01:58:09,191 --> 01:58:10,860
Fear is the mind-killer.

1440
01:58:10,960 --> 01:58:14,697
Fear is the little death
that brings obliteration.

1441
01:58:14,797 --> 01:58:16,298
[rumbling and clanking stop]

1442
01:58:20,302 --> 01:58:23,272
[voices whispering]
See the friend.

1443
01:58:27,042 --> 01:58:29,945
See the friend.

1444
01:58:32,648 --> 01:58:35,451
[Jamis]  The mystery of life
isn't a problem to solve...

1445
01:58:38,654 --> 01:58:41,023
but a reality to experience.

1446
01:58:44,326 --> 01:58:46,562
A process
that cannot be understood

1447
01:58:46,662 --> 01:58:48,898
by stopping it.

1448
01:58:48,998 --> 01:58:51,400
We must move
with the flow of the process.

1449
01:58:52,368 --> 01:58:54,870
We must join it.

1450
01:58:54,970 --> 01:58:56,739
We must flow with it.

1451
01:58:56,839 --> 01:58:58,474
[voices]  Let go.

1452
01:58:58,541 --> 01:59:00,543
Let go.

1453
01:59:02,411 --> 01:59:03,546
[switches click]

1454
01:59:03,646 --> 01:59:05,214
[engine humming]

1455
01:59:29,238 --> 01:59:30,773
[bubbling]

1456
01:59:34,376 --> 01:59:35,878
[servant speaking Harkonnen]

1457
01:59:44,687 --> 01:59:47,289
-[water bubbling]
-[breathes heavily]

1458
01:59:47,389 --> 01:59:51,527
[in English] We chased them
into a Coriolis storm.

1459
01:59:53,028 --> 01:59:55,598
Winds at 800 kilometers
an hour.

1460
02:00:00,269 --> 02:00:02,571
Nothing survives such a storm.

1461
02:00:02,638 --> 02:00:04,073
They're dead.

1462
02:00:05,474 --> 02:00:07,309
It's a certainty.

1463
02:00:12,147 --> 02:00:13,382
[grunts]

1464
02:00:14,316 --> 02:00:16,619
So, it's done. Finally.

1465
02:00:18,754 --> 02:00:20,589
Send word to Giedi Prime

1466
02:00:20,656 --> 02:00:23,492
to begin selling
our spice reserves.

1467
02:00:24,326 --> 02:00:26,428
But slowly.

1468
02:00:26,495 --> 02:00:29,164
We don't want
the price to fall.

1469
02:00:29,265 --> 02:00:30,766
You have no idea
how much it cost me

1470
02:00:30,833 --> 02:00:33,335
to bring such a force
to bear here.

1471
02:00:33,435 --> 02:00:36,305
Now I only have
one requirement.

1472
02:00:36,405 --> 02:00:37,506
Income.

1473
02:00:38,340 --> 02:00:40,142
So, squeeze, Rabban.

1474
02:00:40,909 --> 02:00:42,344
Squeeze hard.

1475
02:00:42,444 --> 02:00:43,812
Yes, Uncle.

1476
02:00:45,414 --> 02:00:46,515
And the Fremen?

1477
02:00:47,650 --> 02:00:49,084
Kill them all.

1478
02:00:52,921 --> 02:00:54,423
[wind gusting]

1479
02:01:04,466 --> 02:01:06,302
[alarm beeping rapidly]

1480
02:01:12,141 --> 02:01:14,109
[Paul] We're above
5,000 meters.

1481
02:01:22,151 --> 02:01:23,485
[engine roars]

1482
02:01:25,888 --> 02:01:27,156
[exhales sharply]

1483
02:01:33,629 --> 02:01:35,397
[ornithopter rattling]

1484
02:01:35,497 --> 02:01:36,899
[Paul grunting]

1485
02:01:46,475 --> 02:01:47,910
[engine roaring]

1486
02:01:48,977 --> 02:01:50,813
[alarm beeping rapidly]

1487
02:01:52,548 --> 02:01:54,583
[sputtering]

1488
02:01:54,683 --> 02:01:56,652
-[metallic rattling]
-[gasping]

1489
02:01:56,719 --> 02:01:57,753
[gasps]

1490
02:01:58,587 --> 02:02:00,656
[alarm continues beeping]

1491
02:02:00,723 --> 02:02:01,690
[switches click]

1492
02:02:01,757 --> 02:02:03,058
[alarm stops beeping]

1493
02:02:07,996 --> 02:02:09,665
[soft rattling]

1494
02:02:16,605 --> 02:02:18,073
[wind whistling]

1495
02:02:22,044 --> 02:02:23,512
[rattling]

1496
02:02:26,248 --> 02:02:28,283
[both gasping]

1497
02:02:31,019 --> 02:02:32,721
[engine whines]

1498
02:02:51,874 --> 02:02:53,809
[Paul] As soon as we land,
run for the rocks.

1499
02:03:04,620 --> 02:03:06,622
[engine accelerates]

1500
02:03:08,157 --> 02:03:09,558
[Lady Jessica whimpering]

1501
02:03:15,264 --> 02:03:17,266
[engine roaring]

1502
02:03:59,775 --> 02:04:01,477
[both panting]

1503
02:04:46,989 --> 02:04:48,824
And breathe through this.

1504
02:05:03,505 --> 02:05:05,707
[rumbling]

1505
02:05:19,021 --> 02:05:21,290
[Paul over mask]  Now
we have to find the Fremen.

1506
02:05:22,858 --> 02:05:24,192
Are you good?

1507
02:05:24,259 --> 02:05:25,627
[Lady Jessica]  Yeah.

1508
02:05:25,727 --> 02:05:27,896
[slow suspenseful music
playing]

1509
02:06:32,494 --> 02:06:34,262
[voices echoing]  Paul...

1510
02:06:40,802 --> 02:06:44,640
Don't be frightened.

1511
02:06:44,706 --> 02:06:47,943
[girl]  Even a little
desert mouse can survive.

1512
02:06:48,977 --> 02:06:52,147
[voices]  Don't be frightened.

1513
02:06:52,214 --> 02:06:54,049
[girl]  You'll need
to face your fears.

1514
02:06:54,149 --> 02:06:55,717
[voices]  A friend...

1515
02:06:55,817 --> 02:06:58,954
A friend will help you.

1516
02:07:00,322 --> 02:07:02,157
Follow the friend.

1517
02:07:04,993 --> 02:07:06,328
[Jamis]
You have much to learn.

1518
02:07:08,530 --> 02:07:11,333
And I will show you
the ways of the desert.

1519
02:07:14,670 --> 02:07:16,238
Come with me.

1520
02:07:22,344 --> 02:07:24,479
[mysterious music playing]

1521
02:07:43,865 --> 02:07:47,602
[Paul]  The  sietch
where Duncan lived

1522
02:07:47,703 --> 02:07:49,871
is somewhere off that way.

1523
02:07:52,040 --> 02:07:55,043
[Lady Jessica]  I can see
greenery over there.

1524
02:07:55,110 --> 02:07:56,278
There.

1525
02:07:56,378 --> 02:07:58,380
[Paul]  That means
Fremen live there.

1526
02:08:02,718 --> 02:08:04,853
We'll cross after dark.

1527
02:08:04,920 --> 02:08:06,922
That's how the Fremen do it.

1528
02:08:09,891 --> 02:08:12,394
[Paul]  We're about to enter
worm territory.

1529
02:08:12,461 --> 02:08:14,296
We can't walk
like regular humans.

1530
02:08:14,396 --> 02:08:15,797
If we do, we're dead.

1531
02:08:15,897 --> 02:08:17,899
We'll have to walk
like the Fremen do.

1532
02:08:17,966 --> 02:08:19,534
It's called a sandwalk.

1533
02:08:19,601 --> 02:08:22,270
At least according
to the filmbooks back home.

1534
02:08:22,370 --> 02:08:23,772
[Lady Jessica]
Yeah. Yeah, okay.

1535
02:08:23,872 --> 02:08:25,407
[Paul]  Okay. Follow me.

1536
02:08:25,474 --> 02:08:27,242
Do the same moves.

1537
02:08:38,553 --> 02:08:40,322
[compass ticking]

1538
02:08:40,422 --> 02:08:42,057
I think this is
the right direction.

1539
02:09:02,177 --> 02:09:04,279
[both grunting]

1540
02:09:16,792 --> 02:09:18,627
[panting]

1541
02:09:26,968 --> 02:09:29,037
[distant rumbling]

1542
02:09:38,213 --> 02:09:39,447
[rumbling fades]

1543
02:10:04,639 --> 02:10:05,707
[Paul]  It's close by.

1544
02:10:06,575 --> 02:10:08,510
Let's get out of here.

1545
02:10:09,344 --> 02:10:12,214
-[thuds]
-Wait.

1546
02:10:12,314 --> 02:10:14,182
-[hollow thudding]
-It's drum sand.

1547
02:10:14,249 --> 02:10:16,051
[wind gusting]

1548
02:10:18,820 --> 02:10:20,755
-[gasps]
-[Paul]  run.

1549
02:10:20,856 --> 02:10:22,991
[tense music playing]

1550
02:10:26,695 --> 02:10:28,396
[Lady Jessica]  Go! Go!

1551
02:10:37,372 --> 02:10:38,573
[grunts]

1552
02:10:39,241 --> 02:10:40,942
[whimpering]

1553
02:11:03,365 --> 02:11:04,599
[rumbling stops]

1554
02:11:09,237 --> 02:11:10,939
[panting]

1555
02:11:12,574 --> 02:11:14,309
[sandworm moans]

1556
02:11:15,577 --> 02:11:16,878
[gasping]

1557
02:11:29,758 --> 02:11:31,559
[rhythmic thumping]

1558
02:11:32,661 --> 02:11:33,728
[thumping stops]

1559
02:11:37,599 --> 02:11:40,435
[soft rhythmic thumping]

1560
02:11:40,502 --> 02:11:41,636
[Paul]  It's a thumper.

1561
02:11:46,942 --> 02:11:48,944
Someone set off a thumper.

1562
02:11:51,012 --> 02:11:52,147
[thumping fades]

1563
02:11:54,849 --> 02:11:56,785
[rhythmic thumping]

1564
02:11:57,752 --> 02:11:58,853
[thumping stops]

1565
02:12:03,491 --> 02:12:05,760
[Lady Jessica]  Paul! Run!

1566
02:12:17,105 --> 02:12:18,673
[both panting]

1567
02:12:20,442 --> 02:12:21,776
How big are they?

1568
02:12:21,843 --> 02:12:23,044
That was insane.

1569
02:12:26,181 --> 02:12:27,682
[groans]

1570
02:12:27,782 --> 02:12:29,317
Someone called it.

1571
02:12:31,686 --> 02:12:32,854
[Lady Jasmine pants]

1572
02:12:39,327 --> 02:12:40,562
[in sign language]

1573
02:12:46,067 --> 02:12:47,702
[pebble clatters]

1574
02:12:51,806 --> 02:12:53,375
[footsteps]

1575
02:13:01,249 --> 02:13:03,818
[Stilgar over mask]
Do not run.

1576
02:13:03,885 --> 02:13:06,521
You will only waste
your body's water.

1577
02:13:07,522 --> 02:13:08,556
Hold.

1578
02:13:16,231 --> 02:13:17,098
Stilgar.

1579
02:13:17,198 --> 02:13:18,767
-[blade rustles]
-Hey!

1580
02:13:18,867 --> 02:13:20,101
You know me. I was there

1581
02:13:20,201 --> 02:13:21,936
when you came
to my father's Council.

1582
02:13:22,037 --> 02:13:23,004
[Stilgar] Oh.

1583
02:13:23,071 --> 02:13:25,106
This is the Duke's son.

1584
02:13:25,206 --> 02:13:26,841
[Jamis] Why are you waiting?

1585
02:13:26,908 --> 02:13:28,777
We need their water.

1586
02:13:28,877 --> 02:13:31,112
[Stilgar] This is the boy
I told you about.

1587
02:13:31,212 --> 02:13:32,447
We can't touch him.

1588
02:13:33,548 --> 02:13:34,949
[woman speaking Fremen]

1589
02:13:36,851 --> 02:13:38,219
[Jamis in English]
They are weaklings.

1590
02:13:38,286 --> 02:13:40,055
[Stilgar] Jamis.

1591
02:13:40,121 --> 02:13:42,023
That was a brave crossing
they made

1592
02:13:42,090 --> 02:13:44,959
in the path of  Shai-Hulud.

1593
02:13:45,060 --> 02:13:48,196
He does not speak
or act like a weakling.

1594
02:13:49,230 --> 02:13:50,932
Nor did his father.

1595
02:13:51,032 --> 02:13:53,635
[Jamis] My thumper
saved his life.

1596
02:13:53,735 --> 02:13:56,204
Go back to reason, Stilgar.

1597
02:13:56,271 --> 02:13:57,972
He's not The One.

1598
02:13:59,707 --> 02:14:00,642
[sighs]

1599
02:14:00,742 --> 02:14:02,410
We have powerful friends.

1600
02:14:02,477 --> 02:14:05,647
You help us off-world,
to Caladan,

1601
02:14:05,747 --> 02:14:06,981
you will be well rewarded.

1602
02:14:07,082 --> 02:14:09,884
What wealth can you offer
beyond the water

1603
02:14:09,951 --> 02:14:11,486
in your flesh?

1604
02:14:14,289 --> 02:14:16,324
[Stilgar] Hmm...

1605
02:14:16,424 --> 02:14:18,059
The boy is young.

1606
02:14:18,126 --> 02:14:20,328
He can learn our ways.

1607
02:14:20,428 --> 02:14:23,064
He may have sanctuary.

1608
02:14:23,131 --> 02:14:25,467
But the woman is untrained...

1609
02:14:28,136 --> 02:14:29,637
and too old to learn.

1610
02:14:33,308 --> 02:14:35,410
[low tense music playing]

1611
02:14:42,450 --> 02:14:43,651
[sniffles]

1612
02:14:48,823 --> 02:14:50,158
[grunting]

1613
02:14:56,164 --> 02:14:57,165
[groans]

1614
02:15:01,002 --> 02:15:03,138
-[both grunt]
-[Stilgar] back, you dogs.

1615
02:15:04,772 --> 02:15:06,975
She'll cut my throat.

1616
02:15:11,946 --> 02:15:14,449
Why didn't you say
you were a weirding woman?

1617
02:15:14,516 --> 02:15:16,184
And a fighter?

1618
02:15:16,284 --> 02:15:18,453
Conversation ran short.

1619
02:15:18,520 --> 02:15:20,722
[Stilgar] Peace, woman.

1620
02:15:20,822 --> 02:15:22,157
Peace.

1621
02:15:22,957 --> 02:15:24,492
I judged hastily.

1622
02:15:28,563 --> 02:15:29,664
[sniffs]

1623
02:15:30,832 --> 02:15:32,467
[Stilgar grunts]

1624
02:15:33,535 --> 02:15:35,303
[speaking Chakobsa]

1625
02:16:03,698 --> 02:16:06,100
[girl in English]  I would not
have let you hurt my friends.

1626
02:16:31,392 --> 02:16:33,962
They say you're the  Mahdi.

1627
02:16:34,062 --> 02:16:35,897
But you look
like a little boy.

1628
02:16:37,398 --> 02:16:38,866
You chose the hardest way up.

1629
02:16:38,933 --> 02:16:40,268
Follow me.

1630
02:16:43,871 --> 02:16:45,573
[Stilgar speaking Chakobsa]

1631
02:16:47,742 --> 02:16:49,310
[in English] Give it to me.

1632
02:16:56,251 --> 02:16:57,952
You will have
your own maula pistol

1633
02:16:58,052 --> 02:16:59,954
when you've earned it.

1634
02:17:00,054 --> 02:17:01,089
Give it to me.

1635
02:17:06,828 --> 02:17:08,963
Chani, take charge
of the newcomers.

1636
02:17:09,063 --> 02:17:11,666
See that they are safe
on the journey. Let's go.

1637
02:17:11,766 --> 02:17:13,167
[Jamis] I will not have them.

1638
02:17:20,108 --> 02:17:21,509
[Stilgar] Jamis,

1639
02:17:21,609 --> 02:17:23,945
I have spoken. Be still.

1640
02:17:24,012 --> 02:17:25,613
[Jamis] You talk like a leader.

1641
02:17:26,614 --> 02:17:28,483
But the strongest leads.

1642
02:17:29,784 --> 02:17:31,586
She bested you.

1643
02:17:32,987 --> 02:17:35,289
I invoke the amtal.

1644
02:17:35,356 --> 02:17:37,792
[Stilgar] You may not challenge
a  Sayyadina.

1645
02:17:37,859 --> 02:17:39,360
Then who will fight
in her name?

1646
02:17:39,460 --> 02:17:42,196
Jamis, don't do this.

1647
02:17:42,297 --> 02:17:44,365
Don't. The night is fading.

1648
02:17:44,465 --> 02:17:47,368
Then the sun
will witness this death.

1649
02:17:47,468 --> 02:17:49,504
Where is her champion?

1650
02:18:00,348 --> 02:18:02,350
I accept her champion.

1651
02:18:25,506 --> 02:18:27,642
[slow dramatic music playing]

1652
02:18:31,846 --> 02:18:33,014
[grunting]

1653
02:18:34,515 --> 02:18:38,419
[voices]  Paul Atreides
must die...

1654
02:18:40,188 --> 02:18:44,892
for  Kwisatz Haderach  to rise.

1655
02:18:47,562 --> 02:18:51,265
Don't be frightened.

1656
02:18:51,366 --> 02:18:52,934
Don't resist.

1657
02:18:59,006 --> 02:19:00,942
When you take a life,

1658
02:19:01,876 --> 02:19:04,011
you take your own.

1659
02:19:12,019 --> 02:19:13,087
[moans]

1660
02:19:27,135 --> 02:19:28,403
[breathing heavily]

1661
02:19:35,777 --> 02:19:38,246
I don't believe
you're the  Lisan al-Gaib.

1662
02:19:39,747 --> 02:19:41,783
But I want you
to die with honor.

1663
02:19:53,261 --> 02:19:56,097
This crysknife was given to me
by my great aunt.

1664
02:19:59,333 --> 02:20:01,736
It's made
from a tooth of  Shai-Hulud.

1665
02:20:01,803 --> 02:20:03,504
The great sandworm.

1666
02:20:05,139 --> 02:20:07,942
This will be a great honor,
for you to die holding it.

1667
02:20:12,246 --> 02:20:14,615
[Jamis shouts]
Where is the Outworlder?

1668
02:20:18,953 --> 02:20:20,855
Jamis is a good fighter.

1669
02:20:21,823 --> 02:20:23,491
He won't let you suffer.

1670
02:20:24,959 --> 02:20:26,594
Chani...

1671
02:20:29,697 --> 02:20:30,765
Um...

1672
02:20:36,704 --> 02:20:37,805
[scoffs]

1673
02:20:38,806 --> 02:20:40,007
Never mind.

1674
02:20:52,653 --> 02:20:54,856
[slow dramatic music
continues]

1675
02:21:35,363 --> 02:21:37,532
May thy knife
chip and shatter.

1676
02:21:45,339 --> 02:21:47,275
You should welcome my blade.

1677
02:21:50,778 --> 02:21:52,547
This world will kill you.

1678
02:21:55,917 --> 02:21:57,451
Quicker this way.

1679
02:22:04,859 --> 02:22:06,561
[spectators speak Chakobsa
in unison]

1680
02:22:08,396 --> 02:22:11,265
-[man speaks Chakobsa]
-[Jamis grunting]

1681
02:22:16,070 --> 02:22:17,872
[breathing heavily]

1682
02:22:37,091 --> 02:22:38,726
-Do you yield?
-[spectators exclaim]

1683
02:22:38,793 --> 02:22:40,895
[Stilgar speaking Chakobsa]

1684
02:22:40,962 --> 02:22:42,830
[Stilgar in English]
The boy doesn't know our rule.

1685
02:22:42,930 --> 02:22:44,165
[yells]

1686
02:22:44,265 --> 02:22:45,833
There's no yielding
under the amtal rule.

1687
02:22:45,933 --> 02:22:47,602
Only death is the test of it.

1688
02:22:47,668 --> 02:22:49,637
[Jamis yelling]

1689
02:22:52,273 --> 02:22:53,941
[both grunting]

1690
02:22:56,010 --> 02:22:57,945
-Is he toying with him?
-No.

1691
02:22:59,280 --> 02:23:00,948
Paul has never killed a man.

1692
02:23:03,017 --> 02:23:04,285
[both grunt]

1693
02:23:06,120 --> 02:23:07,288
[yelling]

1694
02:23:09,523 --> 02:23:11,626
[dramatic lamentation music
playing]

1695
02:23:11,692 --> 02:23:16,130
[voices] Kwisatz Haderach.

1696
02:23:16,197 --> 02:23:17,298
[yelling]

1697
02:23:19,166 --> 02:23:22,203
Kwisatz Haderach.

1698
02:23:22,303 --> 02:23:26,173
Climb up. Rise.

1699
02:23:28,109 --> 02:23:29,143
[stabs]

1700
02:23:29,844 --> 02:23:31,145
[grunts]

1701
02:23:48,162 --> 02:23:49,864
[Jamis groaning]

1702
02:24:02,877 --> 02:24:04,979
[mournful music playing]

1703
02:24:34,241 --> 02:24:36,343
[mournful music continues]

1704
02:25:13,948 --> 02:25:15,549
[speaking Chakobsa]

1705
02:25:18,586 --> 02:25:20,488
[in English]
You're one of us now.

1706
02:25:20,588 --> 02:25:22,423
A life for a life.

1707
02:25:22,490 --> 02:25:24,558
Come with us to  Sietch  Tabr.

1708
02:25:24,625 --> 02:25:25,659
No.

1709
02:25:25,760 --> 02:25:27,294
Paul needs to get off-world.

1710
02:25:27,394 --> 02:25:29,463
You must have ways.
You have smugglers,

1711
02:25:29,563 --> 02:25:30,798
you have ships.

1712
02:25:30,898 --> 02:25:33,000
-[Paul] No.
-[Lady Jessica] You have...

1713
02:25:33,100 --> 02:25:35,169
The Emperor sent us
to this place.

1714
02:25:36,604 --> 02:25:38,339
And my father came,

1715
02:25:39,273 --> 02:25:41,575
not for spice,

1716
02:25:41,642 --> 02:25:43,944
not for the riches,

1717
02:25:44,011 --> 02:25:46,147
but for the strength
of your people.

1718
02:25:49,150 --> 02:25:51,252
My road leads into the desert.

1719
02:25:53,921 --> 02:25:55,289
I can see it.

1720
02:25:57,792 --> 02:25:59,426
If you'll have us,

1721
02:26:00,327 --> 02:26:01,929
we will come.

1722
02:26:08,135 --> 02:26:10,271
[slow dramatic music playing]

1723
02:26:50,544 --> 02:26:52,046
Desert power.

1724
02:26:53,347 --> 02:26:55,049
This is only the beginning.

